            "explanation": "You use 'def' to define a function, 'if/else' to branch the logic, and 'return' to send the final string back out.",
            "hint": "Start the definition with 'def', check the condition with 'if', and give the output back with 'return'."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "mcq",
          "questions": [
            {
              "question": "Which loop is best used when you know the exact number of iterations required?",
              "options": [
