            "question": "Create a dictionary called `employee` with keys 'name' and 'salary'. Store 'Alice' and 50000 as values. Print only the salary.",
            "starterCode": "# Write your code below:\n",
            "solution": "employee = {'name': 'Alice', 'salary': 50000}\nprint(employee['salary'])",
            "language": "python",
            "hint": "Use the key inside square brackets to access a value."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "String Methods",
            "explanation": "",
            "html_code": "<div style='background:#0f172a;color:#e5e7eb;padding:24px;border-radius:12px;font-family:Segoe UI,sans-serif;overflow-x:auto;'><h2 style='text-align:center;color:#60a5fa;margin:0;'>Common Python String Methods</h2><p style='text-align:center;color:#cbd5e1;margin:10px 0 20px;'>Each example shows the string method, its purpose, a code example, and the expected output.</p><table style='width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;'><tr style='background:#2563eb;color:white;'><th style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #475569;'>Method</th><th style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #475569;'>Description</th><th style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #475569;'>Example</th><th style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #475569;'>Output</th></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>upper()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Converts all characters to uppercase.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>text='python'<br>text.upper()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>'PYTHON'</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>lower()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Converts all characters to lowercase.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>text='PyThOn'<br>text.lower()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>'python'</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>title()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Capitalizes the first letter of every word.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>text='hello world'<br>text.title()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>'Hello World'</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>strip()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Removes spaces from both ends.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>text=' hello '<br>text.strip()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>'hello'</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>replace()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Replaces one substring with another.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>text='I like Java'<br>text.replace('Java','Python')</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>'I like Python'</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>split()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Splits a string into a list.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>text='Python AI ML'<br>text.split()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>['Python','AI','ML']</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>join()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Joins list elements into a string.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>' '.join(['I','Love','Python'])</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>'I Love Python'</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>find()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Returns the first matching index.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>text='Python'<br>text.find('t')</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>2</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>startswith()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Checks whether the string starts with a prefix.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>text='Python'<br>text.startswith('Py')</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>True</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>endswith()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Checks whether the string ends with a suffix.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>text='Python'<br>text.endswith('on')</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>True</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>count()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Counts the occurrences of a substring.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>text='banana'<br>text.count('a')</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>3</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-weight:bold;'>len()</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Returns the length of the string.</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas,monospace;'>text='Python'<br>len(text)</td><td style='padding:12px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>6</td></tr></table></div>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "List,Tuple,Set and Dictionary Methods",
            "explanation": "",
            "html_code": "<div style='background:#0f172a;color:#e5e7eb;padding:24px;border-radius:12px;font-family:Segoe UI,sans-serif;overflow-x:auto;'><h2 style='text-align:center;color:#60a5fa;margin:0;'>Common Python Collection Methods</h2><p style='text-align:center;color:#cbd5e1;margin:10px 0 20px;'>Frequently used methods for Python collections with examples and outputs.</p><table style='width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;'><tr style='background:#2563eb;color:white;'><th style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;'>Method</th><th style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;'>Description</th><th style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;'>Example</th><th style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #475569;'>Output</th></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>append()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Adds an item to the end.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data=[1,2]<br>data.append(3)</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>[1,2,3]</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>extend()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Adds multiple items.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data=[1,2]<br>data.extend([3,4])</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>[1,2,3,4]</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>insert()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Inserts an item at a specific position.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data=[1,3]<br>data.insert(1,2)</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>[1,2,3]</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>remove()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Removes the first matching value.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data=[1,2,3]<br>data.remove(2)</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>[1,3]</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>pop()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Removes and returns an item.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data=[1,2,3]<br>data.pop()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>3</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>sort()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Sorts the collection.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data=[3,1,2]<br>data.sort()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>[1,2,3]</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>reverse()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Reverses the order.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data=[1,2,3]<br>data.reverse()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>[3,2,1]</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>count()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Counts occurrences of a value.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data=[1,1,2]<br>data.count(1)</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>2</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>index()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Returns the index of a value.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data=[10,20,30]<br>data.index(20)</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>1</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>clear()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Removes all items.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data.clear()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>[] / {}</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>keys()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Returns all keys.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data.keys()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>dict_keys(['a','b'])</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>values()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Returns all values.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data.values()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>dict_values([1,2])</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>items()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Returns key-value pairs.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data.items()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>dict_items([('a',1),('b',2)])</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>get()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Safely retrieves a value.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data.get('a')</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>1</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>update()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Updates existing data.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data.update({'c':3})</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>{'a':1,'b':2,'c':3}</td></tr><tr><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>popitem()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;'>Removes the last key-value pair.</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;font-family:Consolas;'>data.popitem()</td><td style='padding:10px;border:1px solid #334155;color:#4ade80;'>('b',2)</td></tr></table></div>"
          }
        },
