          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Mini Challenge: Think Like an ML Engineer",
            "explanation": "Congratulations on completing your first end-to-end Machine Learning project!\n\nIn real-world projects, Machine Learning Engineers rarely stop after training a single model. If the model's performance is not satisfactory, they continue experimenting to improve it.\n\n**Your Challenge:**\n• Try different Regression algorithms such as:\n  - Linear Regression\n  - Decision Tree Regressor\n  - Random Forest Regressor\n  - XGBoost Regressor\n  - Gradient Boosting Regressor\n\n• Experiment with different preprocessing techniques:\n  - Better missing value handling\n  - Different outlier treatments\n  - Feature Engineering\n  - Feature Selection\n  - Hyperparameter Tuning\n\n• Compare every model using:\n  - MAE (Mean Absolute Error)\n  - RMSE (Root Mean Squared Error)\n  - R² Score\n\nChoose the model that provides the best balance between accuracy, training time, and prediction performance.\n\n**Industry Insight:** Machine Learning Engineers spend much more time experimenting, comparing models, and improving data quality than simply training one algorithm. Building, evaluating, and continuously improving models is an essential part of every real-world ML project."
