    {
      "id": "M003-dl-lesson-5-cnn-foundations",
      "title": "Image Processing Foundations for Deep Learning",
      "theme": {
        "primary": "#8b5cf6",
        "accent": "#7c3aed"
      },
      "stages": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "What is an Image to a Computer?",
            "explanation": "Until now, we have worked with numbers, tables, and text data. But how does a computer understand images?\nWhen we look at a photo, we see people, animals, buildings, or objects. However, a computer cannot see images the way humans do. For a computer, an image is simply a collection of numbers.\nAn image is made up of tiny squares tiles called **Pixels**. Each pixel stores a numerical value that represents brightness or color.\n[IMAGE:/images/genai/dl/ip1.png]\n`Pixels`\nEach of these individual tiles is called a **pixel** (picture element). It is the smallest unit of an image and holds a mathematical value representing its color intensity (usually between 0 and 255).\n`Resolution`\nResolution is the number of pixels in the grid. An image that is 1920 pixels wide and 1080 pixels tall has a resolution of 1920x1080. \n`Channels (RGB & Grayscale)`\nA grayscale image only needs one number per pixel (0 = Black, 255 = White). But a color image is actually made of three distinct layers stacked on top of each other: **Red, Green, and Blue (RGB)**. A computer mixes the intensity of these three lights to create every color you see.",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"background: #ffffff; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.05); font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; overflow: hidden; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;\"><div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1e293b, #0f172a); padding: 16px; color: white; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; font-size: 16px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-transform: uppercase;\">How Computers See Images 👁️ ➔ 🔢</div><div style=\"padding: 20px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px; align-items: stretch;\"><div style=\"flex: 1; min-width: 250px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center;\"><div style=\"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: #475569; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 20px;\">1. Grayscale (1 Channel)</div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 15px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\"><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 28px); gap: 2px;\"><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #000000; border-radius: 3px;\"></div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #888888; border-radius: 3px;\"></div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 3px;\"></div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 3px;\"></div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #333333; border-radius: 3px;\"></div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #aaaaaa; border-radius: 3px;\"></div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #555555; border-radius: 3px;\"></div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #dddddd; border-radius: 3px;\"></div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #000000; border-radius: 3px;\"></div></div><div style=\"color: #94a3b8; font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold;\">➔</div><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 28px); gap: 2px;\"><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; color: #0f172a; border-radius: 3px;\">0</div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; color: #0f172a; border-radius: 3px;\">136</div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; color: #0f172a; border-radius: 3px;\">255</div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; color: #0f172a; border-radius: 3px;\">255</div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; color: #0f172a; border-radius: 3px;\">51</div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; color: #0f172a; border-radius: 3px;\">170</div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; color: #0f172a; border-radius: 3px;\">85</div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; color: #0f172a; border-radius: 3px;\">221</div><div style=\"width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; font-size: 9px; font-weight: bold; color: #0f172a; border-radius: 3px;\">0</div></div></div><div style=\"margin-top: auto; background: white; padding: 10px 15px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; font-size: 12px; text-align: center; width: 100%;\">1 Pixel = <span style=\"font-family: monospace; background: #f1f5f9; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: bold; color: #334155;\">[150]</span> <br> <span style=\"color: #64748b; font-size: 11px;\">(Just one number: Light Intensity)</span></div></div><div style=\"flex: 1; min-width: 250px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center;\"><div style=\"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: #3b82f6; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 10px;\">2. Color RGB (3 Channels)</div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 120 120\" style=\"width: 120px; height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;\"><polygon points=\"60,115 110,90 60,65 10,90\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2563eb\">B</text><polygon points=\"60,85 110,60 60,35 10,60\" fill=\"rgba(34,197,94,0.15)\" stroke=\"#22c55e\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#16a34a\">G</text><polygon points=\"60,55 110,30 60,5 10,30\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#dc2626\">R</text><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"115\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4\"/></svg><div style=\"margin-top: auto; background: white; padding: 10px 15px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; font-size: 12px; text-align: center; width: 100%;\">1 Pixel = <span style=\"font-family: monospace; background: #fee2e2; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: bold; color: #b91c1c;\">[255, 0, 0]</span> <br> <span style=\"color: #64748b; font-size: 11px;\">(Three stacked layers: Pure Red)</span></div></div></div><div style=\"background: #eff6ff; border-top: 1px solid #bfdbfe; padding: 15px 20px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px;\"><div style=\"font-size: 24px;\">📺</div><div style=\"font-size: 12px; color: #1e3a8a; line-height: 1.5;\"><strong>What is Resolution?</strong> It is the size of the pixel grid. A standard 1080p screen is 1920 pixels wide and 1080 pixels tall. This means a computer must process <strong>2,073,600</strong> numbers (or over 6 million numbers for RGB color!) just to show a single picture.</div></div></div>",
            "example": "Example:\nGrayscale Pixel = [150] (A medium gray)\nColor Pixel = [255, 0, 0] (Maximum Red, No Green, No Blue = Pure Red)"
          }
        },
