        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "The Image Tensor",
            "explanation": "Now that we know images are made of pixels, let's learn how computers store those pixels.\nDeep Learning models cannot directly understand images.Because a computer needs numbers, it stores images as a mathematical structure called a **Tensor**.\nYou can think of an Image Tensor as a 3D spreadsheet or a stack of grids. \n\n**Height × Width × Channels**\nWhen feeding an image into a Deep Learning model, we always define its shape using three dimensions:\n1. **Height:** The number of pixels from top to bottom.\n2. **Width:** The number of pixels from left to right.\n3. **Channels:** The number of color layers (1 for Grayscale, 3 for RGB).\n`Example:`\nA 4K color TV screen has an image shape of: (2160, 3840, 3) Total numbers the computer has to process for just ONE frame: 2160 × 3840 × 3 = 24,883,200 numbers!\n\n**Key Idea:** A single color image is actually three separate grids of numbers. If an image is 28x28 pixels and in color, its tensor shape is (28, 28, 3).",
            "example": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Why Standard Neural Networks Fail Here",
            "explanation": "Now you might be wondering: why can't we simply use the Neural Networks we learned earlier for image data?\nThere is some problem in tradional neural networks that i given below.\n**The Flattening Problem**\nStandard networks require data to be in a flat, 1D line. To feed a 2D image into them, we have to take every row of pixels and line them up end-to-end (a process called **Flattening**).\n\nWhen we flatten an image, **we destroy the spatial structure**. \nA pixel that forms a cat's left ear is no longer next to the pixel that forms the rest of the ear. The network completely loses the understanding of shapes, edges, and objects because it just sees a giant, contextless list of numbers.\n\n**The Solution:** We need a new type of network that respects the 2D grid of an image. We need Convolution.\n**Example :**\nImagine cutting a beautiful painting into 1-inch squares, putting them in a single-file line, and asking someone to guess what the painting was.That's what a Dense Neural Network does to an image!",
            "example": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "The Kernel (The Magnifying Glass)",
            "explanation": "Since traditional Neural Networks struggle with images, we need a smarter approach.\nInstead of looking at the entire image at once, CNNs examine small sections of the image using a tool called a **Kernel** or (**Filter**).\nThink of a Kernel like a magnifying glass moving across a picture.\n\nAs it slides over the image, it looks for important patterns such as Edges,Corners,Curves,Color changes\nThe small area currently being examined is called the **Receptive Field**.\n**Example:** Imagine training an AI to distinguish between cats and dogs. During training, the convolution kernel first learns to detect simple features such as edges, ears, eyes, noses, and fur patterns. As these features pass through deeper convolution layers, the model combines them to recognize more complex patterns, helping it identify whether the image is a cat or a dog.\nLook at the visualization below. It shows how a 3×3 convolution kernel slides across a 5×5 image one step at a time. At each position, the kernel extracts important features and stores the result in the corresponding cell of the 3×3 feature map.\n\n**Key Idea:** A Kernel scans small parts of an image to discover useful visual patterns.\nThe kernel has finished scanning the image. In the next lesson, we'll learn how these results become the Feature Map.",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"position:relative;width:100%;max-width:500px;margin:auto;height:400px;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;box-shadow:0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\"><iframe srcdoc=\"&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;&lt;html lang='en'&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;script src='https://cdn.tailwindcss.com'&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&lt;script src='https://unpkg.com/lucide@latest'&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&lt;style&gt;.cell{transition:all 0.2s;} .active-out{background-color:#c084fc !important; color:white; transform:scale(1.1);}&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body class='bg-slate-50 text-slate-800 font-sans p-0 m-0 h-screen flex flex-col'&gt;&lt;div class='bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-600 to-fuchsia-600 p-3 text-center text-white font-bold text-sm tracking-wide uppercase shadow-sm'&gt;The Sliding Kernel 🔍&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class='flex-grow flex flex-col items-center justify-center p-4'&gt;&lt;div class='flex items-center gap-4 mb-6'&gt;&lt;div class='flex flex-col items-center'&gt;&lt;div class='text-[10px] font-bold text-slate-500 mb-1 uppercase tracking-wider'&gt;5x5 Image Grid&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id='img-grid' class='relative grid grid-cols-5 gap-1 bg-slate-200 p-1 rounded-lg shadow-inner'&gt;&lt;div id='kernel' class='absolute top-1 left-1 w-[84px] h-[84px] border-4 border-pink-500 bg-pink-500/20 rounded-md transition-all duration-300 z-10 pointer-events-none box-border'&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class='flex flex-col items-center justify-center mt-4'&gt;&lt;i data-lucide='arrow-right' class='text-slate-400 w-5 h-5 mb-1'&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;div class='text-[9px] font-bold text-purple-500 bg-purple-100 px-2 py-0.5 rounded'&gt;Filter&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class='flex flex-col items-center'&gt;&lt;div class='text-[10px] font-bold text-slate-500 mb-1 uppercase tracking-wider'&gt;3x3 Feature Map&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id='out-grid' class='grid grid-cols-3 gap-1 bg-purple-100 p-1 rounded-lg border border-purple-200'&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class='flex gap-3'&gt;&lt;button id='btn-step' class='px-4 py-2 bg-white border border-slate-300 rounded-lg shadow-sm text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-50 transition-colors flex items-center gap-2'&gt;&lt;i data-lucide='step-forward' class='w-4 h-4'&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Next Step&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id='btn-play' class='px-4 py-2 bg-purple-600 rounded-lg shadow-md text-sm font-bold text-white hover:bg-purple-700 transition-colors flex items-center gap-2'&gt;&lt;i data-lucide='play' class='w-4 h-4'&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Auto-Scan&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;script&gt;lucide.createIcons();const imgData=[1,1,1,0,0,1,1,1,0,0,1,1,1,0,0,1,1,1,0,0,1,1,1,0,0];const imgGrid=document.getElementById('img-grid');const outGrid=document.getElementById('out-grid');const kernel=document.getElementById('kernel');imgData.forEach(val=&gt;{const div=document.createElement('div');div.className=`w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold rounded-sm ${val===1?'bg-slate-700 text-white':'bg-white text-slate-400'}`;div.innerText=val;imgGrid.appendChild(div);});for(let i=0;i&lt;9;i++){const div=document.createElement('div');div.className='out-cell w-7 h-7 flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold rounded-sm bg-white text-purple-300 cell';div.innerText='?';outGrid.appendChild(div);}let step=0;let playing=false;let timer;function update(){const x=step%3;const y=Math.floor(step/3);kernel.style.transform=`translate(${x*32}px, ${y*32}px)`;const outCells=document.querySelectorAll('.out-cell');outCells.forEach((c,i)=&gt;{c.classList.remove('active-out');if(i===step){c.classList.add('active-out');c.innerText='✓';}});step=(step+1)%9;}document.getElementById('btn-step').addEventListener('click',()=&gt;{clearInterval(timer);playing=false;document.getElementById('btn-play').innerHTML=`&lt;i data-lucide='play' class='w-4 h-4 inline-block align-text-bottom'&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Auto-Scan`;lucide.createIcons();update();});document.getElementById('btn-play').addEventListener('click',(e)=&gt;{if(playing){clearInterval(timer);playing=false;e.currentTarget.innerHTML=`&lt;i data-lucide='play' class='w-4 h-4 inline-block align-text-bottom'&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Auto-Scan`;}else{playing=true;e.currentTarget.innerHTML=`&lt;i data-lucide='pause' class='w-4 h-4 inline-block align-text-bottom'&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Pause`;update();timer=setInterval(update,600);}lucide.createIcons();});update();&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;\" style=\"width:100%;height:100%;border:none;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"></iframe></div>"
          }
        },
