        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Semantic Meaning & Vector Similarity",
            "explanation": "Fantastic! So far, we have learned how to convert words into vectors using Embeddings. But how do computers know that some words have similar meanings?The answer lies in the **Embedding Space**.\n**Embeddings** convert words into vectors (lists of numbers). Words with similar meanings receive similar vectors and are placed close together in a mathematical space called the embedding space.\n\nFor example, 'King', 'Queen', 'Prince', and 'Princess' are closely related concepts, so they appear near each other. Unrelated words such as 'Car' or 'Pizza' appear farther away.\nTo measure how close two words are, NLP models use a metric called Cosine Similarity.\n• High Similarity → Words have related meanings.\n• Low Similarity → Words are less related.\n\nThis is how search engines, recommendation systems, chatbots, and Large Language Models understand meaning instead of simply matching exact words.\nUse the simulator below to select different words and observe how semantically similar words cluster together while unrelated words remain farther away.",
            "html_code": "<iframe style=\"width:100%; min-height:600px; border:none; background:transparent;\" srcdoc=\"<style>body{margin:0;padding:0;display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;min-height:100vh;background:transparent;}</style><div style='font-family:Arial,sans-serif;max-width:900px;margin:auto;padding:20px;background:#fff;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;'><h2 style='margin-top:0;color:#1f2937;'>Word Embedding Explorer</h2><div style='display:flex;justify-content:center;'><svg id='embeddingChart' width='700' height='350' style='border:1px solid #e5e7eb;background:#fafafa;border-radius:8px;'></svg></div><div style='display:flex;justify-content:space-around;margin-top:20px;padding:15px;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb;'><div><div style='font-weight:bold;color:#475569;'>Resulting Vector</div><div id='resultVector' style='margin-top:10px;font-size:18px;'>[80,20]</div></div><div><div style='font-weight:bold;color:#475569;'>Nearest Match</div><div id='nearestWord' style='margin-top:10px;font-size:18px;'>Queen</div></div></div><div style='margin-top:20px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:15px;'><div><label><b>Word A</b></label><select id='wordA' onchange='window.updateEmbedding &amp;&amp; window.updateEmbedding()' style='width:100%;padding:10px;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;'></select></div><div><label><b>Word B</b></label><select id='wordB' onchange='window.updateEmbedding &amp;&amp; window.updateEmbedding()' style='width:100%;padding:10px;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;'></select></div><div style='grid-column:1/span 2;'><label><b>Word C</b></label><select id='wordC' onchange='window.updateEmbedding &amp;&amp; window.updateEmbedding()' style='width:100%;padding:10px;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;'></select></div></div><script>window.words={King:[80,80],Queen:[80,20],Man:[60,80],Woman:[60,20],Python:[-50,-90],Data:[-60,-60],React:[-70,-80],NextJS:[-80,-70]};window.svg=document.getElementById('embeddingChart');window.mapX=function(x){return 350+x*2.5};window.mapY=function(y){return 180-y*1.2};window.distance=function(a,b){return Math.sqrt((a[0]-b[0])*(a[0]-b[0])+(a[1]-b[1])*(a[1]-b[1]))};window.draw=function(result,A,B,C,nearest){const svg=window.svg;if(!svg)return;svg.innerHTML='';for(let i=-100;i<=100;i+=20){svg.innerHTML+=`<line x1='${window.mapX(i)}' y1='20' x2='${window.mapX(i)}' y2='300' stroke='#e5e7eb'/>`;svg.innerHTML+=`<line x1='20' y1='${window.mapY(i)}' x2='680' y2='${window.mapY(i)}' stroke='#e5e7eb'/>`}Object.entries(window.words).forEach(([word,vec])=>{svg.innerHTML+=`<circle cx='${window.mapX(vec[0])}' cy='${window.mapY(vec[1])}' r='5' fill='#2563eb'/>`;svg.innerHTML+=`<text x='${window.mapX(vec[0])+8}' y='${window.mapY(vec[1])-5}' font-size='13'>${word}</text>`});svg.innerHTML+=`<line x1='${window.mapX(B[0])}' y1='${window.mapY(B[1])}' x2='${window.mapX(A[0])}' y2='${window.mapY(A[1])}' stroke='#2563eb' stroke-width='2'/>`;svg.innerHTML+=`<line x1='${window.mapX(B[0])}' y1='${window.mapY(B[1])}' x2='${window.mapX(C[0])}' y2='${window.mapY(C[1])}' stroke='#16a34a' stroke-width='2'/>`;svg.innerHTML+=`<circle cx='${window.mapX(result[0])}' cy='${window.mapY(result[1])}' r='8' fill='none' stroke='#9333ea' stroke-width='3'/>`;svg.innerHTML+=`<text x='${window.mapX(result[0])-18}' y='${window.mapY(result[1])+25}' fill='#9333ea' font-weight='bold'>Result</text>`};window.updateEmbedding=function(){const A=window.words[document.getElementById('wordA').value];const B=window.words[document.getElementById('wordB').value];const C=window.words[document.getElementById('wordC').value];if(!A||!B||!C)return;const result=[A[0]-B[0]+C[0],A[1]-B[1]+C[1]];let nearest='';let min=Infinity;Object.entries(window.words).forEach(([word,vec])=>{const d=window.distance(result,vec);if(d<min){min=d;nearest=word}});document.getElementById('resultVector').innerText='['+Math.round(result[0])+', '+Math.round(result[1])+']';document.getElementById('nearestWord').innerText=nearest;window.draw(result,A,B,C,nearest)};window.populateEmbedding=function(){['wordA','wordB','wordC'].forEach(id=>{const sel=document.getElementById(id);if(!sel)return;sel.innerHTML='';Object.keys(window.words).forEach(word=>{const opt=document.createElement('option');opt.value=word;opt.textContent=word;sel.appendChild(opt)})});document.getElementById('wordA').value='King';document.getElementById('wordB').value='Man';document.getElementById('wordC').value='Woman';window.updateEmbedding()};setTimeout(window.populateEmbedding,100);</script></div>\"></iframe>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "question": "Build a Similar Word Finder. Use the `gensim` library to load a pre-trained embedding model, find the words most semantically related to 'Technology', and perform vector algebra.",
            "starterCode": "import gensim.downloader as api\n\n# Download and load a pre-trained GloVe embedding model\nprint(\"Loading Word Embeddings...\")\nmodel = api.load(\"glove-wiki-gigaword-50\")\n\n# TODO: Use the model to find the top 5 words most similar to 'technology'\nsimilar_words = model.____('technology', topn=5)\n\nprint(\"Words similar to 'technology':\")\nfor word, score in similar_words:\n    print(f\"- {word} ({score:.2f})\")\n\n# TODO: Perform Vector Math: King - Man + Woman\n# Hint: Use positive=['king', 'woman'], negative=['man']\nmath_result = model.____(positive=[____, ____], negative=[____], topn=1)\n\nprint(f\"\\nKing - Man + Woman = {math_result[0][0]}\")",
            "solution": "import gensim.downloader as api\n\n# Download and load a pre-trained GloVe embedding model\nprint(\"Loading Word Embeddings...\")\nmodel = api.load(\"glove-wiki-gigaword-50\")\n\n# TODO: Use the model to find the top 5 words most similar to 'technology'\nsimilar_words = model.most_similar('technology', topn=5)\n\nprint(\"Words similar to 'technology':\")\nfor word, score in similar_words:\n    print(f\"- {word} ({score:.2f})\")\n\n# TODO: Perform Vector Math: King - Man + Woman\n# Hint: Use positive=['king', 'woman'], negative=['man']\nmath_result = model.most_similar(positive=['king', 'woman'], negative=['man'], topn=1)\n\nprint(f\"\\nKing - Man + Woman = {math_result[0][0]}\")",
            "language": "python",
            "hint": "The `gensim` method to find related vectors or perform vector math is `.most_similar()`."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "mcq",
          "questions": [
            {
              "question": "Which of the following best describes the core difference between Bag of Words (BoW) and Word Embeddings?",
              "options": [
