            "Why do LLMs have strict 'context window' limits?"
          ],
          "expectedInsight": "Self-Attention scales quadratically (O(n^2)). If you double the length of the document, the computational cost quadruples! A 100-word sentence requires 10,000 attention calculations. A 100,000-word book requires 10 Billion calculations per layer. This massive memory requirement is the primary limitation of modern Transformers and why strict 'Context Windows' exist."
        },
        {
