            {
              "text": "Tune the model to maximize Recall. We absolutely must catch every single Stop Sign, even if it means the AI occasionally triggers the brakes for a red billboard.",
              "outcome": "Correct! In life-or-death scenarios, a False Negative (missing a stop sign) is fatal. A False Positive (braking for a billboard) is annoying but safe. You must maximize Recall!",
              "score": 100
            },
            {
              "text": "Tune the model for Perplexity.",
              "outcome": "Incorrect. Perplexity is for text generation models, not binary classification tasks like Stop Sign detection.",
              "score": 10
