        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Building a Simple Chatbot",
            "explanation": "Excellent! So far, we've learned how to send a single prompt to an LLM and receive a response. But real AI applications like ChatGPT don't process just one message—they maintain an entire conversation.\n\nHow does a chatbot remember what we said earlier?\n\nThe answer is **Conversation History**.\n\nInstead of sending only the latest user message, a chatbot stores every message exchanged between the user and the AI. Whenever the user asks a new question, the complete conversation history is sent to the model. This allows the model to understand the context and generate meaningful responses.\n\nLet's understand the workflow of a simple chatbot.\n\n**Chatbot Workflow:**\n\n• User sends the first message.\n\n• The message is added to the conversation history.\n\n• The complete conversation history is sent to the LLM.\n\n• The model generates a response.\n\n• The response is also added to the conversation history.\n\n• The process repeats for every new user message.\n\nFor example:\n\n**User:** What is the capital of France?\n\n**AI:** Paris.\n\n**User:** What famous tower is located there?\n\n**AI:** The Eiffel Tower.\n\n**User:** When was it built?\n\n**AI:** It was completed in 1889.\n\nNotice that the user never mentioned 'Eiffel Tower' again in the third question. The chatbot answered correctly because it remembered the previous conversation.\n\nIn the following example, we'll build a simple terminal-based chatbot using the OpenAI API.",
            "example": "from openai import OpenAI\n\nclient = OpenAI(api_key='YOUR_API_KEY')\n\nmessages = []\n\nprint('Simple AI Chatbot (type exit to quit)')\n\nwhile True:\n    user_input = input('You: ')\n\n    if user_input.lower() == 'exit':\n        break\n\n    # Store user message\n    messages.append({\n        'role': 'user',\n        'content': user_input\n    })\n\n    # Send conversation history\n    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n        model='gpt-4o-mini',\n        messages=messages\n    )\n\n    ai_reply = response.choices[0].message.content\n\n    print('AI:', ai_reply)\n\n    # Store AI response\n    messages.append({\n        'role': 'assistant',\n        'content': ai_reply\n    })",
            "tip": "The secret behind every chatbot is the conversation history. If you don't send previous messages back to the model, it won't remember earlier parts of the conversation."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "question": "Build a chatbot that sends a user message to GPT and prints the response.",
            "starterCode": "from openai import OpenAI\n\nclient = OpenAI(api_key='YOUR_API_KEY')\n\n# Complete the chatbot\n",
            "solution": "from openai import OpenAI\n\nclient = OpenAI(api_key='YOUR_API_KEY')\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n model='gpt-4o-mini',\n messages=[{'role':'user','content':'Hello GPT'}]\n)\n\nprint(response.choices[0].message.content)",
            "language": "python",
            "hint": "Use client.chat.completions.create()",
            "explanation": "The chatbot sends a prompt and receives an AI-generated response."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Building a Text Summarizer",
            "explanation": "Excellent! We've built our first chatbot. Now let's build another practical LLM application—a **Text Summarizer**.\n\nImagine you have a 20-page research paper, a long business report, or a lengthy news article. Reading the entire document can take a lot of time. Instead, we can ask an LLM to read the content and generate a shorter version while preserving the most important information.\n\nThis process is called **Text Summarization**.\n\nText summarization is widely used in news applications, research tools, document management systems, legal software, and AI assistants to help users quickly understand long documents.\n\nLet's understand how a text summarizer works.\n\n**Workflow:**\n\n• Provide the document or long text.\n\n• Write a prompt instructing the LLM to summarize it.\n\n• Send both the prompt and document to the LLM.\n\n• The LLM identifies the key information.\n\n• The model generates a concise summary.\n\nOne of the biggest advantages of using an LLM is that you don't need to build a separate summarization model. Simply changing the prompt allows the same LLM to perform the task.\n\nIn the following example, we'll build a simple text summarizer using the OpenAI API.",
            "example": "from openai import OpenAI\n\nclient = OpenAI(api_key='YOUR_API_KEY')\n\ntext = '''\nArtificial Intelligence is transforming industries by automating repetitive tasks, improving decision-making, and enabling intelligent applications. Today, AI is widely used in healthcare, finance, education, manufacturing, and many other fields to improve efficiency and solve complex problems.\n'''\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model='gpt-4o-mini',\n    messages=[\n        {\n            'role': 'user',\n            'content': f'Summarize the following text in 3 bullet points:\\n\\n{text}'\n        }\n    ]\n)\n\nsummary = response.choices[0].message.content\n\nprint(summary)\n# Expected Output:\n# • Artificial Intelligence automates repetitive tasks and improves decision-making.\n# • AI is widely used in industries such as healthcare, finance, education, and manufacturing.\n# • AI helps organizations increase efficiency and solve complex real-world problems.",
            "tip": "Be specific in your prompt. For example, ask the model to summarize the text in one paragraph, five bullet points, or under 100 words to get more consistent results."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "question": "Build an AI-powered text summarization application using the OpenAI API. Given a long article or document, generate a concise summary that captures the key information.",
