              ],
              "answer": 1,
              "explanation": "Format constraints remove natural text conversational elements from output buffers, enabling applications to directly pass data structures into JSON parsers or databases without syntax failures."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "scenario",
          "title": "The Broken CRM System",
          "description": "You are deploying an automated system that reads client feedback data records from a web dashboard and drafts email replies automatically. During beta testing, the model occasionally inserts pleasantries like 'Sure, here is that email draft for you:' or writes responses that sound overly apologetic and defensive when handling complaints. This upsets corporate users. How do you re-engineer the system prompt architecture to handle this reliably?",
          "choices": [
