    {
      "id": "M006-prompt-eng-05",
      "title": "Prompt Engineering for Real Applications",
      "theme": {
        "primary": "#10b981",
        "accent": "#047857"
      },
      "stages": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Real-World Application: Building AI Chatbots",
            "explanation": "Excellent! So far, we've learned how to write effective prompts, guide the model's reasoning, and generate structured outputs. Now let's see how these techniques are used to build real AI applications.\n\nOne of the most common applications of Large Language Models is an **AI Chatbot**. Unlike a single prompt-and-response interaction, a chatbot must communicate with users over many messages while maintaining a consistent personality, following company policies, and handling unexpected questions.\n\nTo achieve this, developers use a carefully designed **System Prompt**. The System Prompt acts as the chatbot's permanent set of instructions. Before responding to every user message, the model first follows these rules.\n\nIn industry, a chatbot's system prompt usually defines:\n\n• **Role** – Who the assistant is (Customer Support Agent, Banking Assistant, HR Assistant, Medical Assistant, etc.).\n\n• **Personality** – The communication style, such as friendly, professional, empathetic, or concise.\n\n• **Rules and Boundaries** – What the assistant is allowed and not allowed to do. For example, never reveal confidential information, never provide legal advice, or never invent answers.\n\n• **Fallback Behavior** – What the assistant should do when it doesn't know the answer. Instead of hallucinating, it may politely ask the user to contact support or escalate the request to a human agent.\n\nTake a look at the production-style system prompt below. Notice how the chatbot receives clear instructions about its role, behavior, security rules, and how to respond when users try to break those rules.\n\nThis approach is used in customer support chatbots, banking assistants, healthcare assistants, HR bots, e-commerce support, and enterprise AI applications.\nNow, let's look at an example of a system prompt used for a customer support chatbot.",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"font-family:Consolas,monospace;background:#0f172a;color:#e2e8f0;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #334155;\"><h3 style=\"margin-top:0;color:#38bdf8;\">#Example of Bank Customer support Chatbot System Prompt</h3><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#e2e8f0;\">SYSTEM\n\nYou are Acme Bank's AI Customer Support Assistant.\n\nROLE\n- Help customers with banking questions.\n\nPERSONALITY\n- Friendly, professional, and concise.\n\nRULES\n- Never reveal confidential information.\n- Never guess account details.\n- Never provide legal or financial advice.\n- If authentication is required, ask the customer to sign in.\n\nFALLBACK\n- If you don't know the answer, politely say so and direct the customer to customer support.\n\nESCALATION\n- If the request involves fraud, account closure, or disputes, transfer the conversation to a human agent.</pre></div>",
            "example": "# Industry Chatbot System Prompt\nsystem_prompt = '''\nYou are an AI Customer Support Assistant for an online shopping platform.\n\nYour responsibilities:\n- Answer questions about orders, shipping, returns, and refunds.\n- Be polite, professional, and concise.\n- Never make up order information.\n- If you don't know the answer, tell the customer you cannot verify the information.\n- If the customer requests account deletion or payment disputes, transfer the conversation to a human support agent.\n'''\n\nmessages = [\n    {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system_prompt},\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"My package hasn't arrived yet. Can you help me?\"}\n]\n\nresponse = llm.invoke(messages)\nprint(response)\n\n# Expected Output:\n# I'd be happy to help. Could you please provide your order ID so I can assist you with your shipment status?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Real-World Application: Content Generation",
            "explanation": "Excellent! In the previous lesson, we learned how Prompt Engineering is used to build AI chatbots. Another major real-world application of Large Language Models is **Content Generation**.\n\nBusinesses use AI every day to create blog articles, marketing campaigns, product descriptions, emails, social media posts, advertisements, newsletters, landing pages, and documentation. However, simply asking the AI to **'Write a blog'** usually produces generic content that sounds robotic and lacks a clear purpose.\n\nProfessional AI Engineers solve this problem by writing detailed prompts that clearly define the content requirements before generation begins.\n\nA production-quality content generation prompt typically includes:\n\n• **Target Audience** – Who will read the content?\n• **Objective** – What is the purpose? (Educate, Sell, Inform, Entertain, Persuade)\n• **Tone** – Professional, Friendly, Technical, Humorous, etc.\n• **Length** – Number of words or paragraphs.\n• **Writing Style** – Short paragraphs, storytelling, bullet points, examples, etc.\n• **Keywords or SEO Requirements** – Important search terms to include.\n• **Call to Action (CTA)** – What should the reader do after reading?\n\nTake a look at the comparison below. The prompt on the left provides almost no guidance, so the AI generates generic content. The prompt on the right includes detailed instructions, resulting in content that is engaging, audience-focused, and aligned with business goals.\n\nThis approach is widely used in marketing teams, content management systems, e-commerce platforms, SEO tools, advertising agencies, and AI writing assistants.\n\nLet's examine an example prompt designed for AI-powered content generation.",
            "tip": "When generating content, don't just describe the topic. Also specify the audience, objective, tone, format, length, keywords, and desired call to action. The more context you provide, the better the generated content will match your requirements.",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;padding:20px;border-radius:16px;\"><h3 style=\"text-align:center;margin-top:0;color:#1e293b;\">Generic Prompt vs Production Prompt</h3><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;\"><div style=\"flex:1;padding:12px;background:#fef2f2;border-radius:8px;border-left:4px solid #ef4444;\"><b>❌ Generic Prompt</b><p style=\"font-size:12px;color:#475569;\">Write a blog about Artificial Intelligence.</p><hr><p style=\"font-size:12px;color:#991b1b;\">Result: Generic, repetitive, and lacks a clear audience.</p></div><div style=\"flex:1;padding:12px;background:#ecfdf5;border-radius:8px;border-left:4px solid #10b981;\"><b>✅ Production Prompt</b><p style=\"font-size:12px;color:#475569;\">Write an 800-word beginner-friendly blog about Artificial Intelligence for college students. Use a conversational tone, include headings, real-world examples, and finish with a call to action.</p><hr><p style=\"font-size:12px;color:#065f46;\">Result: Audience-focused, engaging, and ready for publishing.</p></div></div></div>",
            "example": "# Industry Content Generation Prompt\nsystem_prompt = '''\nYou are an expert content writer.\n\nWrite high-quality content that follows these rules:\n- Target Audience: College students\n- Objective: Educate beginners about Artificial Intelligence\n- Tone: Friendly and conversational\n- Length: 700-800 words\n- Structure: Title, introduction, headings, conclusion\n- Include 3 real-world examples\n- End with a call to action\n'''\n\nuser_prompt = \"Write a blog about Artificial Intelligence.\"\n\nresponse = llm.invoke([\n    {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system_prompt},\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user_prompt}\n])\n\nprint(response)\n\n# Expected Output:\n# A well-structured beginner-friendly blog with a title,\n# clear headings, practical examples, and a concluding\n# call to action."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Real-World Application: Information Extraction & Summarization",
            "explanation": "Excellent! So far, we've learned how Prompt Engineering powers chatbots and content generation. Another major real-world application of Large Language Models is **Information Extraction** and **Summarization**.\n\nEvery day, businesses generate huge amounts of unstructured text, including meeting transcripts, emails, customer support conversations, legal contracts, research papers, and financial reports. Reading all this information manually is time-consuming and inefficient.\n\nAI helps solve this problem in two different ways.\n\n**Summarization** focuses on reducing large amounts of text into a shorter version while preserving the most important information. For example, an hour-long meeting transcript can be summarized into a few key points.\n\n**Information Extraction** is different. Instead of creating a shorter version, the AI identifies and extracts specific pieces of information such as names, dates, phone numbers, invoice amounts, action items, deadlines, or important decisions.\n\nIn real-world applications, developers don't simply ask the AI to 'summarize this document.' Instead, they provide clear instructions about what information should be extracted and how the output should be formatted. This produces more reliable and consistent results.\n\nTake a look at the example below. The prompt on the left is vague and may produce different summaries each time. The prompt on the right clearly specifies exactly what information should be extracted, making the output much more useful for business applications.\n\nThis approach is widely used in meeting assistants, CRM systems, legal document analysis, healthcare records, customer support platforms, HR systems, financial reporting, and document processing applications.\n\n**Now, let's look at a real industry-style prompt for information extraction and summarization.**",
            "tip": "Instead of asking the AI to 'summarize this document,' specify exactly what information you need and define the expected output format. Clear extraction instructions produce more consistent and reliable results.",
            "example": "# Information Extraction Prompt\nsystem_prompt = '''\nYou are an AI meeting assistant.\n\nRead the meeting transcript and extract ONLY the following information:\n\n1. Meeting Summary\n2. Key Decisions\n3. Action Items (Owner - Task)\n4. Deadlines\n5. Risks or Blockers\n\nReturn the output in Markdown.\n'''\n\nuser_prompt = \"\"\"\nMeeting Transcript:\nThe team decided to launch the mobile application on August 15.\nRahul will complete API integration.\nPriya will prepare the user documentation.\nThe biggest risk is delayed client approval.\n\"\"\"\n\nresponse = llm.invoke([\n    {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system_prompt},\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user_prompt}\n])\n\nprint(response)\n\n# Expected Output:\n# ## Meeting Summary\n# The team finalized the mobile app launch plan.\n#\n# ### Key Decisions\n# - Launch scheduled for August 15.\n#\n# ### Action Items\n# - Rahul - Complete API integration.\n# - Priya - Prepare user documentation.\n#\n# ### Deadlines\n# - Mobile app launch: August 15.\n#\n# ### Risks\n# - Delayed client approval."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "title": "Hands-On: AI Travel Assistant",
            "difficulty": "Medium",
            "question": "Create a System Prompt for an AI Travel Assistant that recommends destinations, hotels, and attractions. It must never book tickets or guarantee prices.",
            "starterCode": "from openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\n# TODO: Write the system prompt\nsystem_prompt = \"\"\"\n[Your System Prompt Here]\n\"\"\"\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n    messages=[\n        {\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":system_prompt},\n        {\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Book me the cheapest flight to Paris tomorrow.\"}\n    ]\n)\n\nprint(response.choices[0].message.content)",
            "language": "python",
            "expected_output": "The assistant should recommend travel options but explain that it cannot make bookings or guarantee prices.",
            "hint": "Restrict the assistant from making reservations or confirming prices.",
            "solution": "from openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\nsystem_prompt = \"\"\"\nRole: You are an AI Travel Assistant.\n\nRules:\n1. Recommend destinations, hotels, restaurants, and attractions.\n2. Never book flights or hotels.\n3. Never guarantee ticket prices or availability.\n4. Recommend users visit the official booking website.\n\"\"\"\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n    messages=[\n        {\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":system_prompt},\n        {\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Book me the cheapest flight to Paris tomorrow.\"}\n    ]\n)\n\nprint(response.choices[0].message.content)"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "title": "Hands-On: Product Description Generator",
            "difficulty": "Medium",
            "question": "Write a prompt that generates an engaging product description for a wireless noise-cancelling headphone. The description should target online shoppers, highlight the main features, include a benefits section, and end with a persuasive call to action.",
            "starterCode": "from openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\n# TODO: Write the prompt\nprompt = \"\"\"\n[Your Prompt Here]\n\"\"\"\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n    messages=[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":prompt}]\n)\n\nprint(response.choices[0].message.content)",
            "language": "python",
            "expected_output": "An e-commerce product description highlighting features, customer benefits, and ending with a call to action.",
            "hint": "Include audience, tone, product features, structure, and call to action.",
            "solution": "from openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\nprompt = \"\"\"\nGenerate an e-commerce product description.\n\nProduct: Wireless Noise-Cancelling Headphones\nAudience: Online shoppers\nTone: Friendly and persuasive\nInclude:\n1. Product title\n2. Short introduction\n3. Key features\n4. Customer benefits\n5. Call to action\n\"\"\"\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n    messages=[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":prompt}]\n)\n\nprint(response.choices[0].message.content)"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "title": "Hands-On: Research Paper Summarizer",
            "difficulty": "Medium",
            "question": "You are building an AI Research Assistant. Write a prompt that summarizes a research paper into four sections: Overview, Key Findings, Limitations, and Future Work. The summary should be concise and easy for college students to understand.",
            "starterCode": "from openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\npaper = '''\nLarge Language Models (LLMs) have shown remarkable performance across various NLP tasks, including question answering, summarization, and code generation. However, these models require significant computational resources for training and inference. Researchers are exploring techniques such as quantization, knowledge distillation, and parameter-efficient fine-tuning to reduce computational costs while maintaining model performance.\n'''\n\n# TODO: Write the summarization prompt\nprompt = \"\"\"\n[Your Prompt Here]\n\"\"\"\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n    messages=[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":prompt + paper}]\n)\n\nprint(response.choices[0].message.content)",
            "language": "python",
            "expected_output": "The AI should generate a summary with four sections: Overview, Key Findings, Limitations, and Future Work.",
            "hint": "Instead of simply asking the AI to summarize the paper, specify the exact sections and the target audience.",
            "solution": "from openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\npaper = '''\nLarge Language Models (LLMs) have shown remarkable performance across various NLP tasks, including question answering, summarization, and code generation. However, these models require significant computational resources for training and inference. Researchers are exploring techniques such as quantization, knowledge distillation, and parameter-efficient fine-tuning to reduce computational costs while maintaining model performance.\n'''\n\nprompt = '''\nSummarize the following research paper.\n\nTarget Audience: College students\n\nReturn the summary using the following sections:\n1. Overview\n2. Key Findings\n3. Limitations\n4. Future Work\n\nKeep the explanation simple and concise.\n'''\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n    messages=[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":prompt + paper}]\n)\n\nprint(response.choices[0].message.content)"
