          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Prompting for Software Developers",
            "explanation": "Software developers use AI assistants like ChatGPT, Gemini, and Claude to write code, debug errors, explain unfamiliar codebases, optimize algorithms, generate unit tests, create documentation, and even review pull requests. Instead of asking vague questions like 'Fix my code,' developers provide the programming language, framework, expected behavior, error messages, and constraints. The more context they provide, the more accurate and useful the generated solution becomes.\nLet's look at the prompt below and understand how it is structured.",
            "example": "You are a Senior Python Developer with expertise in FastAPI.\n\nContext:\nI am developing a FastAPI application and need help debugging my code.\n\nYour tasks:\n1. Identify all errors in the code.\n2. Explain why each error occurs.\n3. Provide the best solution.\n4. Rewrite the corrected code.\n5. Suggest any improvements for readability, performance, or security.\n6. Follow Python and FastAPI best practices.\n\nResponse Format:\n- Issues Found\n- Explanation\n- Corrected Code\n- Recommendations\n\nCode:\n[paste your code here]"
          }
        },
