            "title": "Build It: Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)",
            "difficulty": "Medium",
            "question": "Write a Python function that takes two ranked lists of document IDs (one from Dense search, one from BM25) and calculates their combined RRF scores. Use the standard constant k=60.",
            "starterCode": "def calculate_rrf(dense_ranks, sparse_ranks, k=60):\n    rrf_scores = {}\n    # dense_ranks is a list of doc_ids ordered by rank [docA, docB, docC]\n    # TODO: Calculate RRF score for each document\n    pass\n\ndense = ['doc_A', 'doc_B', 'doc_C']\nsparse = ['doc_C', 'doc_A', 'doc_B']\nprint(calculate_rrf(dense, sparse))",
            "language": "python",
            "expected_output": "{'doc_A': 0.0325, 'doc_C': 0.0325, 'doc_B': 0.0320}",
            "hint": "Loop through each list. The score to add is 1 / (k + rank + 1). Remember lists are 0-indexed!",
            "solution": "def calculate_rrf(dense_ranks, sparse_ranks, k=60):\n    rrf_scores = {}\n    \n    for rank, doc_id in enumerate(dense_ranks):\n        rrf_scores[doc_id] = rrf_scores.get(doc_id, 0.0) + 1.0 / (k + rank + 1)\n        \n    for rank, doc_id in enumerate(sparse_ranks):\n        rrf_scores[doc_id] = rrf_scores.get(doc_id, 0.0) + 1.0 / (k + rank + 1)\n        \n    return rrf_scores\n\ndense = ['doc_A', 'doc_B', 'doc_C']\nsparse = ['doc_C', 'doc_A', 'doc_B']\nprint(calculate_rrf(dense, sparse))"
          }
