    {
      "id": "M004-nlp-lesson-9-practice",
      "title": "Practice Project",
      "theme": {
        "primary": "#e11d48",
        "accent": "#be123c"
      },
      "stages": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Step 1: Practice Project - Build an AI-Powered ShopSphere Customer Support Chatbot",
            "explanation": "🎉 Congratulations! You have completed the theoretical concepts of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). Now it's time to apply everything you've learned by building a complete real-world AI application from scratch.\n\nIn this practice project, you will build an **AI-Powered Customer Support Chatbot** for an e-commerce company called **ShopSphere** using **LangChain, ChromaDB, HuggingFace Embeddings, Groq, FastAPI, and HTML**.\n\n---\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nImagine you have recently joined **ShopSphere** as an **AI Engineer**.\n\nEvery day, thousands of customers contact the support team with similar questions.\n\nSome of the most frequently asked questions are:\n\n• How do I track my order?\n• Can I cancel my order?\n• How long does delivery take?\n• Is shipping free? etc.\n\nCurrently, customer support agents answer these questions manually, which takes time and increases operational costs.\n\nTo solve this problem, ShopSphere wants to build an **AI-powered Customer Support Chatbot** that can automatically answer customer questions using the company's FAQ document.\n\nInstead of training a brand-new Large Language Model, we will build a **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)** system. Whenever a customer asks a question, the chatbot will search the company's knowledge base, retrieve the most relevant information, and generate an accurate response using an LLM.\n\nBy the end of this project, you will have built a complete AI chatbot that can answer customer questions just like a real customer support assistant.\n\n## Dataset Overview\n\nFor this project, we will use a PDF knowledge base named **ShopSphere_Ecommerce_FAQ_Knowledge_Base.pdf**.\n\n📄 **Dataset:** [ShopSphere_Ecommerce_FAQ_Knowledge_Base.pdf](/images/genai/rag/datasets/faqs_docs.pdf)\n\nThe PDF contains frequently asked customer support questions and answers covering topics such as:\n\n• Order Tracking\n• Shipping\n• Payments\n• Returns & Refunds\n• Customer Support etc.\n\nThis PDF serves as the **knowledge base** for our RAG chatbot. Whenever a customer asks a question, the chatbot retrieves the most relevant information from this document before generating an accurate response\n\n## Create the Project Folder\n\nOpen **Visual Studio Code**.\n\nCreate a new project folder named:`shopsphere-rag-chatbot`\nOpen this folder inside VS Code.\n\nNext, open the integrated terminal and create a virtual environment.\n\n### Windows\n\n```bash\npython -m venv venv\n#Activate the virtual environment:\n venv\\Scripts\\activate\n```\n\n### macOS / Linux\n\n```bash\npython3 -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate\n```\n\nAfter activation, your terminal should display the virtual environment name before the command prompt.\n\n---\n\n## Create the Project Structure\n\nInside the project folder, create the following file structure.\n\n```text\n📁shopsphere-rag-chatbot/\n│\n├── venv/\n│\n├── data/\n│   └── ShopSphere_Ecommerce_FAQ_Knowledge_Base.pdf\n│\n├── rag.py\n├── app.py\n├── index.html\n├── requirements.txt\n└── .env\n```\n\n• data/ → Stores the chatbot knowledge base PDF.\n• rag.py → Implements the complete RAG pipeline.\n• app.py → Creates the FastAPI backend and chat API.\n• index.html → Provides the chatbot web interface.\n• requirements.txt → Lists all required Python libraries.\n• .env → Stores API keys and other secrets securely.\n\n## Technologies Used\n\nThroughout this project, we will use the following technologies:\n\n• LangChain — Build the complete RAG pipeline.\n\n• HuggingFace Embeddings — Convert document chunks into numerical vectors.\n\n• ChromaDB — Store embeddings and perform semantic similarity search.\n\n• Groq — Generate fast AI responses using an open-source Large Language Model.\n\n• FastAPI — Create the backend REST API.\n\n• HTML, CSS, and JavaScript — Build a simple chatbot user interface.\nIn the next lesson, we'll begin implementing the heart of this application by building the complete **Knowledge Base** loading the PDF, splitting it into chunks, generating embeddings, storing them in ChromaDB, and creating a Retriever."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Step 2: Build the Knowledge Base using LangChain and ChromaDB",
            "explanation": "Now it's time to build the heart of our RAG application—the **Knowledge Base**.\n\nInstead of writing all the code in one place, we'll organize our application into small reusable functions. Each function will perform one specific task, making the code cleaner, easier to understand, and simpler to maintain.\n\nWe'll implement the complete knowledge base inside a single file named `rag.py`.\nBefore we start building the knowledge base, let's install all the required libraries for this stage.\nOpen the terminal in Visual Studio Code and run the following command:\n```bash\npip install langchain langchain-community langchain-huggingface langchain-chroma chromadb sentence-transformers pypdf\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 1 — Import Required Libraries\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_community.document_loaders import PyPDFLoader\nfrom langchain.text_splitter import RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter\nfrom langchain_huggingface import HuggingFaceEmbeddings\nfrom langchain_chroma import Chroma\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2 — Load the ShopSphere PDF\n\nCreate a function that loads the PDF and returns the extracted documents.\n\n```python\ndef load_documents():\n    loader = PyPDFLoader(\n        \"data/ShopSphere_Ecommerce_FAQ_Knowledge_Base.pdf\"\n    )\n\n    documents = loader.load()\n    return documents\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3 — Split the Documents into Chunks\n\nCreate another function that receives the loaded documents and splits them into smaller overlapping chunks.\n\n```python\ndef split_documents(documents):\n\n    splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(\n        chunk_size=500,\n        chunk_overlap=100\n    )\n\n    chunks = splitter.split_documents(documents)\n\n    return chunks\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 4 — Create the Embedding Model\n\nNext, initialize the HuggingFace embedding model.\n\n```python\ndef get_embedding_model():\n\n    embedding_model = HuggingFaceEmbeddings(\n        model_name=\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\"\n    )\n\n    return embedding_model\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 5 — Create the Vector Database\n\nNow store all document chunks inside ChromaDB.\n\n```python\ndef create_vector_database(chunks, embedding_model):\n\n    vector_db = Chroma.from_documents(\n        documents=chunks,\n        embedding=embedding_model,\n        persist_directory=\"./chroma_db\"\n    )\n\n    return vector_db\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 6 — Create the Retriever\n\nFinally, create the Retriever that will search the vector database.\n\n```python\ndef create_retriever(vector_db):\n\n    retriever = vector_db.as_retriever(\n        search_kwargs={\"k\":3}\n    )\n\n    return retriever\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 7 — Build the Knowledge Base\n\nFinally, call all the functions in sequence to prepare the complete knowledge base.\n\n```python\ndef build_knowledge_base():\n\n    documents = load_documents()\n\n    chunks = split_documents(documents)\n\n    embedding_model = get_embedding_model()\n\n    vector_db = create_vector_database(\n        chunks,\n        embedding_model\n    )\n\n    retriever = create_retriever(vector_db)\n\n    return retriever\n```\n\nOur knowledge base is now ready. Whenever a customer asks a question, the Retriever will search the ShopSphere FAQ and return the most relevant document chunks.\n\nIn the next lesson, we'll connect this Retriever with Groq's Large Language Model to build the complete RAG pipeline."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Step 3: Build the Complete RAG Pipeline using Groq",
            "explanation": "Excellent! Our Knowledge Base is now ready. The Retriever can search the ShopSphere FAQ and return the most relevant document chunks. However, it cannot generate conversational responses.\n\nThe next step is to connect the Retriever with a Large Language Model (LLM). In this project, we'll use **Groq** to generate fast AI-powered answers.\n\nWe'll continue working inside the existing **rag.py** file.\n\nBefore writing the code, install the required libraries.\n\n```bash\npip install langchain-groq python-dotenv\n```\n\nOr add them to **requirements.txt** and install them using:\n\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Import the Required Libraries\n\nFirst, import the Groq model, Prompt Template, Retrieval Chain utilities, and environment variable loader.\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_groq import ChatGroq\nfrom langchain_core.prompts import ChatPromptTemplate\nfrom langchain.chains.combine_documents import create_stuff_documents_chain\nfrom langchain.chains import create_retrieval_chain\n\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\nimport os\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Load the Groq API Key\n\nLoad the environment variables and read the Groq API key from the `.env` file.\n\n```python\nload_dotenv()\n\nGROQ_API_KEY = os.getenv(\"GROQ_API_KEY\")\n```\n\nYour `.env` file should contain:\n\n```text\nGROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Create the Groq Language Model\n\nCreate a function that initializes and returns the Groq language model.\n\n```python\ndef get_llm():\n\n    llm = ChatGroq(\n        groq_api_key=GROQ_API_KEY,\n        model_name=\"llama-3.3-70b-versatile\",\n        temperature=0\n    )\n\n    return llm\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Create the Prompt Template\n\nNow create a prompt template that combines the retrieved context with the user's question.\n\n```python\ndef get_prompt():\n\n    prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(\n        \"\"\"\nYou are a helpful customer support assistant for ShopSphere.\n\nAnswer the user's question using only the provided context.\n\nIf the answer cannot be found in the context, reply:\n'I couldn't find this information in the ShopSphere knowledge base.'\n\nContext:\n{context}\n\nQuestion:\n{input}\n\"\"\"\n    )\n\n    return prompt\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Create the Document Chain\n\nNext, combine the language model with the prompt template.\n\n```python\ndef create_document_chain(llm, prompt):\n\n    document_chain = create_stuff_documents_chain(\n        llm,\n        prompt\n    )\n\n    return document_chain\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 6: Create the Retrieval Chain\n\nNow connect the Retriever with the Document Chain to build the complete RAG pipeline.\n\n```python\ndef create_rag_chain(retriever, document_chain):\n\n    rag_chain = create_retrieval_chain(\n        retriever,\n        document_chain\n    )\n\n    return rag_chain\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 7: Build the Complete RAG Pipeline\n\nFinally, call all the functions in sequence to prepare the complete RAG chatbot.\n\n```python\ndef build_rag_pipeline():\n\n    retriever = build_knowledge_base()\n\n    llm = get_llm()\n\n    prompt = get_prompt()\n\n    document_chain = create_document_chain(\n        llm,\n        prompt\n    )\n\n    rag_chain = create_rag_chain(\n        retriever,\n        document_chain\n    )\n\n    return rag_chain\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 8: Test the RAG Pipeline\n\nLet's verify that our chatbot is working correctly.\n\n```python\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n\n    rag_chain = build_rag_pipeline()\n\n    response = rag_chain.invoke(\n        {\n            \"input\": \"How do I track my order?\"\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(response[\"answer\"])\n```\n\n**Example Output**\n\n```text\nYou can track your order by opening My Orders and selecting Track Package.\n```\n\nNow our complete RAG pipeline is ready. It retrieves relevant information from the ShopSphere knowledge base, sends that context to Groq, and generates a natural language response.\n\nIn the next lesson, we'll build **app.py** using FastAPI, expose the RAG pipeline as a REST API, and test it using Swagger UI."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Step 4: Build the FastAPI Backend and Test the Chatbot using Swagger",
            "explanation": "Excellent! Our RAG pipeline is now complete. It can retrieve relevant information from the ShopSphere knowledge base and generate intelligent responses using Groq.\n\nHowever, the chatbot currently runs only inside a Python program. To allow websites, mobile applications, or any other software to communicate with it, we need to expose it as a REST API.\n\nIn this step, we'll create a FastAPI backend that accepts customer questions, sends them to our RAG pipeline, and returns AI-generated responses in JSON format.\n\nOpen **app.py**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Import the Required Libraries\n\nFirst, import FastAPI, Pydantic, and the RAG pipeline.\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nfrom rag import build_rag_pipeline\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Create the FastAPI Application\n\nCreate a FastAPI application.\n\n```python\napp = FastAPI(\n    title=\"ShopSphere Chatbot API\"\n)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Load the RAG Pipeline\n\nLoad the RAG pipeline once when the application starts.\n\n```python\nrag_chain = build_rag_pipeline()\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Create the Request Model\n\nCreate a Pydantic model to receive the customer's question.\n\n```python\nclass ChatRequest(BaseModel):\n    question: str\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Create the Response Model\n\nCreate a response model that returns the chatbot's answer.\n\n```python\nclass ChatResponse(BaseModel):\n    answer: str\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 6: Create the Chat API\n\nCreate a POST endpoint named `/chat`.\n\n```python\n@app.post(\n    \"/chat\",\n    response_model=ChatResponse\n)\ndef chat(request: ChatRequest):\n\n    response = rag_chain.invoke(\n        {\n            \"input\": request.question\n        }\n    )\n\n    return ChatResponse(\n        answer=response[\"answer\"]\n    )\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 7: Run the FastAPI Server\n\nOpen the terminal and run the following command.\n\n```bash\nuvicorn app:app --reload\n```\n\nOnce the server starts successfully, FastAPI automatically generates an interactive API documentation page called **Swagger UI**.\n\nOpen your browser and visit:\n\n```text\nhttp://127.0.0.1:8000/docs\n```\n\nYou should see a page similar to the following.\n[IMAGE:/images/genai/rag/pp.png]\n### Step 8: Test the Chatbot\n\nClick the **POST /chat** endpoint, choose **Try it out**, enter a customer question, and click **Execute**.\n\n**Example Request**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"question\": \"How do I track my order?\"\n}\n```\n\n**Example Response**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"You can track your order by opening My Orders and selecting Track Package.\"\n}\n```\n\nOur FastAPI backend is now complete. It exposes the RAG chatbot as a REST API that can be accessed from any frontend application.\n\nIn the next lesson, we'll build **index.html**, where users can interact with the chatbot through a clean and responsive web interface."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Step 5: Build a Simple HTML Chatbot Interface",
            "explanation": "Excellent! Our FastAPI backend is now ready, and the chatbot can answer questions through the **/chat** API.\n\nThe next step is to build a simple user interface so customers can interact with the chatbot from their web browser.\n\nCreate a new file named **index.html**.\n\nFor now, we'll build only the frontend layout using **HTML**. The question and answer shown below are **static** and are used only to design the chatbot interface. We haven't connected it to our FastAPI backend yet.\n\nCopy the following HTML code and save it as **index.html**.\n```python\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background:#eef2f7;padding:40px;display:flex;justify-content:center;\">\n    <div style=\"width:420px;background:white;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 8px 25px rgba(0,0,0,.12);overflow:hidden;\">\n        <div style=\"background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:18px;text-align:center;font-size:24px;font-weight:bold;\">\n            ShopSphere AI Chatbot\n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"height:360px;padding:20px;background:#f8fafc;overflow:auto;\">\n            <div style=\"background:#e0f2fe;padding:12px 16px;border-radius:12px;max-width:85%;margin-bottom:18px;\">\n                👋 Hello! Welcome to ShopSphere. How can I help you today?\n            </div>\n\n            <div style=\"background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:12px 16px;border-radius:12px;max-width:80%;margin-left:auto;margin-bottom:18px;\">\n                How do I track my order?\n            </div>\n\n            <div style=\"background:#e0f2fe;padding:12px 16px;border-radius:12px;max-width:85%;\">\n                You can track your order by opening <b>My Orders</b> and clicking <b>Track Package</b>.\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"display:flex;padding:16px;border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb;background:white;\">\n            <input type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Type your question...\" style=\"flex:1;padding:12px 14px;border:1px solid #d1d5db;border-radius:8px;font-size:15px;outline:none;\">\n            <button style=\"margin-left:10px;background:#2563eb;color:white;border:none;padding:12px 22px;border-radius:8px;font-weight:bold;cursor:pointer;\">Send</button>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>\n```\nAfter running the index.html file, the chatbot interface will look like this.\n\n[IMAGE:/images/genai/rag/pp1.png]\n\nIn the next lesson, we'll use JavaScript to connect this interface to our FastAPI **/chat** API and make the chatbot fully interactive."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Step 6: Connect the HTML Chatbot with the FastAPI Backend",
            "explanation": "Excellent! Our chatbot interface is now ready. However, it still displays static messages because it isn't connected to the FastAPI backend.\n\nIn this step, we'll make the chatbot fully interactive.\n\nOpen the existing **index.html** file.\n\nIn the following code snippets, we'll update the HTML and add JavaScript that sends the user's question to the **/chat** API using the Fetch API.\n\n```python\n<div style='background:#1e1e1e;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;font-family:Consolas,monospace;color:#d4d4d4;line-height:1.5;overflow:auto;'>\n    <span style='color:#569CD6;'>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span>\n    &lt;html lang='en'&gt;\n\n    &lt;head&gt;\n        &lt;meta charset='UTF-8'&gt;\n        &lt;meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0'&gt;\n        &lt;title&gt;ShopSphere AI Chatbot&lt;/title&gt;\n\n        <span style='color:#6A9955;'>&lt;!-- CSS Styles --&gt;</span>\n        &lt;style&gt;\n            <span style='color:#808080;'>/* Chat UI Styling */</span>\n        &lt;/style&gt;\n    &lt;/head&gt;\n\n    &lt;body&gt;\n        <span style='color:#6A9955;'>&lt;!-- Chat Container --&gt;</span>\n        &lt;div class='chat-container'&gt;\n            &lt;div class='header'&gt;🤖 ShopSphere AI Chatbot&lt;/div&gt;\n\n            &lt;div class='chat-box' id='chatBox'&gt;\n                &lt;div class='bot-message'&gt;\n                    👋 Hello! Welcome to ShopSphere.&lt;br&gt;\n                    How can I help you today?\n                &lt;/div&gt;\n            &lt;/div&gt;\n\n            &lt;div class='input-area'&gt;\n                &lt;input type='text' id='question' placeholder='Type your question...'&gt;\n                &lt;button onclick='sendMessage()'&gt;Send&lt;/button&gt;\n            &lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n\n        <span style='color:#6A9955;'>&lt;!-- JavaScript --&gt;</span>\n        &lt;script&gt;\n            <span style='color:#808080;'>// Sends user messages to the FastAPI backend and displays AI responses.</span>\n        &lt;/script&gt;\n    &lt;/body&gt;\n\n    &lt;/html&gt;\n</div>\n```\n\nWhenever the user clicks the **Send** button, JavaScript sends the question to the FastAPI backend. The backend processes the request using the RAG pipeline and returns an AI-generated response, which is automatically displayed in the chat window.\n\nBefore testing the chatbot, make sure the FastAPI server is running.\n\n```bash\nuvicorn app:app --reload\n```\n\nAfter completing all the snippets and saving **index.html**, open it in your browser. The chatbot will now communicate with the FastAPI backend instead of displaying hardcoded responses.\n\nThe completed chatbot interface will look similar to the following.\n[IMAGE:/images/genai/rag/pp2.png]\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Step 8: Project Wrap-Up and What's Next",
            "explanation": "🎉 Congratulations! You have successfully completed your first end-to-end Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) project.\n\nThroughout this project, you learned how to:\n\n✔ Build a knowledge base from PDF documents.\n\n✔ Generate embeddings using HuggingFace.\n\n✔ Store vectors in ChromaDB.\n\n✔ Retrieve relevant documents using semantic search.\n\n✔ Build a complete RAG pipeline using Groq.\n\n✔ Create a FastAPI backend.\n\n✔ Design an HTML chatbot interface.\n\n✔ Connect the frontend with the FastAPI backend to build a fully functional AI chatbot.\n\nThis project provides a strong foundation for building AI-powered customer support assistants and other document-based applications.\n\n## Project Improvements\n\nNow that you've completed the project, try enhancing it by implementing some additional features:\n\n• Add conversation history.\n\n• Stream AI responses for a better user experience.\n\n• Support multiple PDF documents.\n\n• Add user authentication.\n\n• Store chat history in a database.\n\n• Deploy the chatbot to a cloud platform.\n\nThese improvements will help you build a more scalable and production-ready RAG application.\n\n## Try It Yourself: Vectorless RAG\n\nAs your next challenge, try building the same chatbot without using a vector database. This approach is called **Vectorless RAG**.\n\nBuild the project on your own and compare it with the vector-based RAG you created in this project. Notice the differences in architecture, retrieval process, performance, and use cases.\n\nIn the next project, we'll build a complete Vectorless RAG system together and explore when it is a better choice than traditional vector-based RAG.\n\nCongratulations once again on completing this project. Keep building and exploring more real-world AI applications!"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
