      "stages": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "The Business Challenge",
            "explanation": "Congratulations! You have joined 'TechCorp' as an Jr.AI Engineer.\n\nThe company has thousands of documents spread across PDFs, HR policies, employee handbooks, product manuals, FAQs, and support guides. Employees constantly ask the same questions such as:\n\n• What is the leave policy?\n• How do I submit expenses?\n• What is the VPN setup process?\n• How do I reset my company password?\n\nThe HR and IT teams are overwhelmed with repetitive questions.\n\n**Your Mission:** Build an Enterprise Knowledge Assistant using RAG that can search company documents and answer employee questions accurately."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Industrial RAG Workflow",
            "explanation": "`1.Document Collection` → Gather PDFs, FAQs, manuals, and internal documents.\n`2.Document Loading` → Extract text from files.\n`3.Text Cleaning` → Remove headers, footers, and irrelevant content.\n`4.Chunking` → Split documents into smaller chunks.\n`5.Embedding Generation` → Convert chunks into vectors.\n`6.Vector Storage` → Store vectors inside a Vector Database.\n`7.Query Embedding` → Convert user question into an embedding.\n`8.Retrieval` → Find similar chunks.\n`9.Context Injection` → Add retrieved chunks into the prompt.\n`10.LLM Generation` → Generate the final answer.\n`11.Evaluation` → Verify retrieval quality and answer quality.\n`12.Deployment` → Deploy as an internal company chatbot.\n\n**Workflow:**\nDocuments → Chunking → Embeddings → Vector DB → Retrieval → Context Injection → LLM → Answer"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Project Setup",
            "explanation": "In this mini project, you'll build a complete Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline from scratch. Instead of writing all the code in a single file, we'll organize our project just like real-world AI applications.\n\n### Step 1: Create the Project Folder\n• Create a new folder named `Simple_RAG_Project`.\n\n### Step 2: Open VS Code\n• Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code.\n\n### Step 3: Create a Virtual Environment\nOpen the integrated terminal and run `python -m venv venv`.\n\nActivate it:\n• Windows: `venv\\Scripts\\activate`\n• Mac/Linux: `source venv/bin/activate`\n\n### Step 4: Install Required Libraries\nRun `pip install sentence-transformers chromadb openai pypdf`.\n\n### Step 5: Project Files\nCreate the following Python files:\n• `ingestion.py`\n• `retrieval.py`\n• `main.py`\n\n### Dataset\nA sample **FAQ PDF** is provided in the below `hyperlink` download and use. Use this document as your knowledge base while building the RAG application.\n\nThroughout the next three coding exercises, you'll implement each file step by step using our built-in IDE. After completing all three files, simply run `main.py` to execute the complete RAG pipeline and ask questions about the FAQ document.",
            "html_code": "<div style=\"padding:18px;background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:10px;text-align:center;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;\"><h3 style=\"margin-top:0;color:#1e3a8a;\">📄 Project Dataset</h3><p style=\"color:#475569;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;\">Use the provided FAQ document as the knowledge base for building your RAG application.</p><a href=\"/FAQs.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" download style=\"display:inline-block;margin-top:10px;padding:10px 18px;background:#2563eb;color:white;text-decoration:none;border-radius:6px;font-weight:bold;\">⬇ Download FAQ Document</a></div>"
