        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "What's Next? From Local RAG to Production",
            "explanation": "Congratulations! You have successfully built a complete Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) application. Your system can now ingest documents, retrieve the most relevant context, and generate answers using an LLM.\n\n**Typical Industry Workflow:**\n• Store thousands or millions of documents inside a Vector Database such as ChromaDB, Pinecone, Weaviate, or Milvus.\n• Build a REST API using frameworks like **FastAPI**, **Flask**, or **Django**.\n• Users submit questions through a web or mobile application.\n• The API retrieves the most relevant documents, builds the RAG prompt, sends it to the LLM, and returns the generated answer.\n• Deploy the application to cloud platforms such as **AWS**, **Azure**, **Google Cloud**, or **Render** so users can access it from anywhere.\n• Continuously update the knowledge base by ingesting new documents without retraining the LLM.\n\n**What's Coming Next:** In the upcoming modules, you'll learn advanced RAG techniques such as Hybrid Search, Query Expansion, Reranking, Parent-Child Retrieval, Graph RAG, Agentic RAG, Self-RAG, and production deployment of scalable RAG systems."
