        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Project: AI Content Generator",
            "explanation": "An AI Content Generator uses multiple providers to create, review, and optimize content. It combines the strengths of different models in a pipeline: fast drafting with a cheap model, quality review with a premium model, and SEO optimization with a specialized tool.",
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "sevenPoint",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "number": 1,
                    "title": "Architecture Overview",
                    "body": "User provides a topic and content type (blog, tweet thread, LinkedIn post). The system generates a draft, reviews it for quality, optimizes for SEO, and outputs the final polished content with metadata."
                  },
                  {
                    "number": 2,
                    "title": "Step 1: Research & Outline",
                    "body": "Use Gemini (long context) to ingest reference materials and generate a structured outline. Gemini's 2M context window means it can read dozens of competitor articles simultaneously."
                  },
                  {
                    "number": 3,
                    "title": "Step 2: Draft Generation",
                    "body": "Use GPT-4o-mini (fast and cheap) to generate the first draft based on the outline. The system prompt includes the target audience, tone, and word count constraints."
                  },
                  {
                    "number": 4,
                    "title": "Step 3: Quality Review",
                    "body": "Use Claude (best reasoning) to review the draft for factual accuracy, logical flow, grammar, and engagement. Claude outputs structured feedback with specific edit suggestions."
                  },
                  {
                    "number": 5,
                    "title": "Step 4: SEO Optimization",
                    "body": "Use a specialized tool (or another LLM call) to add meta descriptions, optimize headings, suggest internal links, and ensure keyword density is within best practices."
                  },
                  {
                    "number": 6,
                    "title": "Step 5: Multi-Format Output",
                    "body": "The system outputs the content in multiple formats: full blog post (Markdown), tweet thread (280-char segments), LinkedIn post (with emoji and hashtags), and email newsletter version."
                  },
                  {
                    "number": 7,
                    "title": "Cost Optimization",
                    "body": "By using cheap models for high-volume tasks (drafting) and expensive models only for critical tasks (review), the pipeline achieves premium quality at 1/5th the cost of using GPT-4o for everything."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "speed_quiz",
