            "question": "Write a function called 'load_and_validate' that loads a JSONL file line by line, validates each entry has 'instruction' and 'output' keys, and returns only valid entries as a list. Skip invalid entries and print a warning.",
            "starterCode": "import json\n\ndef load_and_validate(filepath: str) -> list:\n    '''Load JSONL file and return only valid entries.'''\n    valid_entries = []\n    with open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n        for i, line in enumerate(f):\n            entry = json.loads(line)\n            # Validate and append\n            ___\n    return valid_entries",
            "solution": "import json\n\ndef load_and_validate(filepath: str) -> list:\n    '''Load JSONL file and return only valid entries.'''\n    valid_entries = []\n    with open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n        for i, line in enumerate(f):\n            entry = json.loads(line)\n            if 'instruction' in entry and 'output' in entry:\n                valid_entries.append(entry)\n            else:\n                print(f'Warning: Skipping invalid entry at line {i}')\n    return valid_entries",
