            "difficulty": "Hard",
            "question": "Write a function called 'evaluate_model_outputs' that takes a list of test_cases (each with 'prompt' and 'expected_quality' keys) and a list of model_outputs (strings). For each pair, create a judge prompt that asks GPT-4 to rate the response 1-10 on helpfulness. Return the average score as a float. Use the OpenAI client.",
            "starterCode": "from openai import OpenAI\nimport json\n\ndef evaluate_model_outputs(test_cases: list, model_outputs: list) -> float:\n    '''Evaluate model outputs using LLM-as-a-Judge. Returns average score.'''\n    client = OpenAI()\n    scores = []\n    \n    for case, output in zip(test_cases, model_outputs):\n        judge_prompt = f\"\"\"Rate this AI response 1-10 on helpfulness.\n\nUser asked: {case['prompt']}\nAI responded: {output}\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object: {{\"score\": X, \"reason\": \"...\"}}\"\"\"\n        \n        response = client.chat.completions.create(\n            model='gpt-4o-mini',\n            messages=[{'role': 'user', 'content': judge_prompt}],\n            response_format={'type': 'json_object'}\n        )\n        \n        result = json.loads(response.choices[0].message.content)\n        scores.append(result['score'])\n    \n    # Return average score\n    ___",
            "solution": "from openai import OpenAI\nimport json\n\ndef evaluate_model_outputs(test_cases: list, model_outputs: list) -> float:\n    '''Evaluate model outputs using LLM-as-a-Judge. Returns average score.'''\n    client = OpenAI()\n    scores = []\n    \n    for case, output in zip(test_cases, model_outputs):\n        judge_prompt = f\"\"\"Rate this AI response 1-10 on helpfulness.\n\nUser asked: {case['prompt']}\nAI responded: {output}\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object: {{\"score\": X, \"reason\": \"...\"}}\"\"\"\n        \n        response = client.chat.completions.create(\n            model='gpt-4o-mini',\n            messages=[{'role': 'user', 'content': judge_prompt}],\n            response_format={'type': 'json_object'}\n        )\n        \n        result = json.loads(response.choices[0].message.content)\n        scores.append(result['score'])\n    \n    return sum(scores) / len(scores)",
            "hint": "Return sum(scores) / len(scores) for the average score.",
            "explanation": "LLM-as-a-Judge automates subjective evaluation at scale. GPT-4 rates each response on a numeric scale, and averaging gives you a single quality metric. The JSON response format ensures clean parsing. This technique is used by every major AI lab for model evaluation.",
