            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "The Message System: Speaking the LLM's Language",
            "explanation": "You've just called an LLM with a simple string — and even swapped providers! But here's the thing: in the real world, you don't just send a single string to the AI. You need to give it a PERSONALITY, send multi-turn conversations, and handle complex interactions.\n\n**🧒 The Script Analogy:**\n\nImagine you're directing a movie. You don't just tell the actor \"say something\" — you give them a SCRIPT with clear roles:\n\n• **Director's notes** (system instructions) — \"You're playing a pirate captain. Be dramatic.\"\n• **Other actor's line** (user message) — \"Captain, we've spotted land!\"\n• **Your actor's response** (AI message) — \"Arrr! Full speed ahead, ye scallywags!\"\n\nWithout the script, the actor is just guessing. With it, they know exactly who they are and how to respond.\n\nLangChain's Message system works the same way. Instead of plain strings, you send structured messages with clear roles:\n\n<img src=\"/images/m11 langchain/m11_message_system.png\" alt=\"LangChain Message System Analogy\" />\n\n**📋 The Four Message Types:**\n• **SystemMessage** — Sets the AI's persona and rules. The \"director's notes\" before the show starts.\n• **HumanMessage** — What the user says. This is the input.\n• **AIMessage** — The model's response. You rarely create these manually.\n• **ToolMessage** — Results from tool/function execution (we'll cover this later).\n\n**Using Messages in Practice:**\n```python\nfrom langchain_core.messages import SystemMessage, HumanMessage\n\nmessages = [\n    SystemMessage(content='You are a pirate. Always respond in pirate speak.'),\n    HumanMessage(content='What is Python?')\n]\n\nresponse = model.invoke(messages)\n# 'Arrr! Python be a fine programming language, matey!'\n```\n\n**🔄 Multi-Turn Conversations:**\nHere's the powerful part — just pass the FULL conversation history:\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_core.messages import SystemMessage, HumanMessage, AIMessage\n\nmessages = [\n    SystemMessage(content='You are a helpful teacher.'),\n    HumanMessage(content='What is 2+2?'),\n    AIMessage(content='2+2 equals 4!'),\n    HumanMessage(content='And what about 2+3?')\n]\n```\n\nThe model sees the entire conversation and can reference previous exchanges. This is how you build context-aware chatbots — by passing the full message history with each call.\n\n**⚠️ IMPORTANT:** LLMs have NO memory between calls. Every `.invoke()` is a fresh start. The ONLY reason the model \"remembers\" previous messages is because YOU resend them every time. We'll learn how to automate this with Memory later in this module.\n\nLet's practice creating messages with code."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
