            "question": "Create a State TypedDict for a research agent. It should have:\n1. messages: a list with the add_messages reducer (Annotated)\n2. search_query: a string (no reducer — default overwrite)\n3. sources: a list (no reducer)\n\nStore it in a class called 'ResearchState'.",
            "starterCode": "from typing import TypedDict, Annotated\nfrom langgraph.graph.message import add_messages\n\nclass ResearchState(TypedDict):\n    # messages with add_messages reducer\n    ___\n    # search_query as a string\n    ___\n    # sources as a list\n    ___",
            "solution": "from typing import TypedDict, Annotated\nfrom langgraph.graph.message import add_messages\n\nclass ResearchState(TypedDict):\n    messages: Annotated[list, add_messages]\n    search_query: str\n    sources: list",
            "hint": "Use Annotated[list, add_messages] for messages. The other fields are plain type hints: str and list.",
