        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "language": "python",
            "title": "Complete Agent with Tool Loop",
            "difficulty": "Hard",
            "question": "Build a complete tool-calling agent graph. Define a router function 'should_use_tool' that checks if the last message in state['messages'] has tool_calls. If yes, return 'tools'. If no, return 'end'. Then wire up the graph with:\n1. Add nodes: 'agent' and 'tools'\n2. Set entry point to 'agent'\n3. Add conditional edges from 'agent' using should_use_tool\n4. Add standard edge from 'tools' back to 'agent' (the loop!)\n5. Compile the graph.",
            "starterCode": "from typing import TypedDict, Annotated\nfrom langgraph.graph import StateGraph, END\nfrom langgraph.graph.message import add_messages\n\nclass State(TypedDict):\n    messages: Annotated[list, add_messages]\n\ndef agent_node(state):\n    # Placeholder: would call LLM\n    return {'messages': ['Agent response']}\n\ndef tool_node(state):\n    # Placeholder: would execute tools\n    return {'messages': ['Tool result']}\n\n# Router function\ndef should_use_tool(state):\n    ___\n\n# Build the graph\ngraph_builder = StateGraph(State)\ngraph_builder.add_node('agent', agent_node)\ngraph_builder.add_node('tools', tool_node)\ngraph_builder.set_entry_point('agent')\n\n# Add conditional edges from 'agent'\n___\n\n# Add loop: tools -> agent\n___\n\n# Compile\ngraph = graph_builder.compile()",
            "solution": "from typing import TypedDict, Annotated\nfrom langgraph.graph import StateGraph, END\nfrom langgraph.graph.message import add_messages\n\nclass State(TypedDict):\n    messages: Annotated[list, add_messages]\n\ndef agent_node(state):\n    return {'messages': ['Agent response']}\n\ndef tool_node(state):\n    return {'messages': ['Tool result']}\n\ndef should_use_tool(state):\n    last_message = state['messages'][-1]\n    if hasattr(last_message, 'tool_calls') and last_message.tool_calls:\n        return 'tools'\n    return 'end'\n\ngraph_builder = StateGraph(State)\ngraph_builder.add_node('agent', agent_node)\ngraph_builder.add_node('tools', tool_node)\ngraph_builder.set_entry_point('agent')\n\ngraph_builder.add_conditional_edges(\n    'agent',\n    should_use_tool,\n    {'tools': 'tools', 'end': END}\n)\n\ngraph_builder.add_edge('tools', 'agent')\n\ngraph = graph_builder.compile()",
            "hint": "The router checks for tool_calls on the last message. Use add_conditional_edges('agent', should_use_tool, {'tools': 'tools', 'end': END}). Loop back with add_edge('tools', 'agent').",
            "explanation": "This is the fundamental agent loop pattern:\n1. Agent node calls the LLM\n2. Router checks: does the LLM want to use a tool?\n3. If yes → execute tool → loop BACK to agent\n4. If no → END (return final answer)\n\nThis loop continues until the LLM is satisfied with its answer.",
            "concepts": [
              "Agent Loop",
              "Conditional Edges",
              "Tool Calling",
              "Graph Compilation"
            ],
            "validation": {
              "type": "regex_match",
              "pattern": "add_conditional_edges.*agent.*should_use_tool"
            },
            "hints": [
