        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "language": "python",
            "title": "Full Conversational Agent with Memory",
            "difficulty": "Hard",
            "question": "Build a complete chatbot with persistent memory. Create the State with messages (add_messages), define a chatbot node that returns a response, build the graph with MemorySaver, and invoke it TWICE with the same thread_id to show memory working. Store the second result in 'result2'.",
            "starterCode": "from typing import TypedDict, Annotated\nfrom langgraph.graph import StateGraph\nfrom langgraph.graph.message import add_messages\nfrom langgraph.checkpoint.memory import MemorySaver\n\n# 1. Define State\nclass State(TypedDict):\n    messages: Annotated[list, add_messages]\n\n# 2. Define chatbot node\ndef chatbot(state):\n    last_msg = str(state['messages'][-1])\n    return {'messages': [f'You said: {last_msg}']}\n\n# 3. Build and compile graph with memory\ngraph_builder = StateGraph(State)\n___\n\n# 4. Invoke twice with same thread_id\nconfig = {'configurable': {'thread_id': 'demo_session'}}\nresult1 = graph.invoke({'messages': [('human', 'My name is Alice')]}, config=config)\nresult2 = graph.invoke({'messages': [('human', 'What did I just say?')]}, config=config)",
            "solution": "from typing import TypedDict, Annotated\nfrom langgraph.graph import StateGraph\nfrom langgraph.graph.message import add_messages\nfrom langgraph.checkpoint.memory import MemorySaver\n\nclass State(TypedDict):\n    messages: Annotated[list, add_messages]\n\ndef chatbot(state):\n    last_msg = str(state['messages'][-1])\n    return {'messages': [f'You said: {last_msg}']}\n\ngraph_builder = StateGraph(State)\ngraph_builder.add_node('chatbot', chatbot)\ngraph_builder.set_entry_point('chatbot')\ngraph_builder.set_finish_point('chatbot')\n\ncheckpointer = MemorySaver()\ngraph = graph_builder.compile(checkpointer=checkpointer)\n\nconfig = {'configurable': {'thread_id': 'demo_session'}}\nresult1 = graph.invoke({'messages': [('human', 'My name is Alice')]}, config=config)\nresult2 = graph.invoke({'messages': [('human', 'What did I just say?')]}, config=config)",
            "hint": "Add the 'chatbot' node, set entry/finish points, create MemorySaver(), and compile with checkpointer=checkpointer.",
            "explanation": "Because both invoke() calls use the same thread_id ('demo_session'), the second call has access to the FULL conversation from the first call. The checkpointer saves and restores state automatically.",
            "concepts": [
              "Full Agent",
              "Memory",
              "Thread ID",
              "Conversation Persistence"
            ],
