            "title": "Your First Tool-Calling Agent (OpenAI)",
            "difficulty": "Medium",
            "question": "Complete the tool-calling agent below. You need to:\n1. Define a `tools` list with a single tool: `get_weather` that takes a `city` parameter (string)\n2. Pass the `tools` list to `client.chat.completions.create()`\n3. Check if `response.choices[0].message.tool_calls` exists",
            "starterCode": "from openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\n# Step 1: Define the tools list\ntools = [{\n    'type': 'function',\n    'function': {\n        'name': '___',\n        'description': '___',\n        'parameters': {\n            'type': 'object',\n            'properties': {\n                '___': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The city name'}\n            },\n            'required': ['___']\n        }\n    }\n}]\n\n# Step 2: Call the API with tools\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model='gpt-4o-mini',\n    messages=[{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the weather in London?'}],\n    ___=tools\n)\n\n# Step 3: Check for tool calls\nmessage = response.choices[0].message\nif message.___:\n    print('Tool call detected:', message.tool_calls[0].function.name)",
            "solution": "from openai import OpenAI\nclient = OpenAI()\n\ntools = [{\n    'type': 'function',\n    'function': {\n        'name': 'get_weather',\n        'description': 'Get current weather for a city',\n        'parameters': {\n            'type': 'object',\n            'properties': {\n                'city': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The city name'}\n            },\n            'required': ['city']\n        }\n    }\n}]\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model='gpt-4o-mini',\n    messages=[{'role': 'user', 'content': 'What is the weather in London?'}],\n    tools=tools\n)\n\nmessage = response.choices[0].message\nif message.tool_calls:\n    print('Tool call detected:', message.tool_calls[0].function.name)",
            "hint": "The tool name should be 'get_weather', the parameter name should be 'city', pass tools= to the create() call, and check message.tool_calls.",
            "explanation": "This is the real OpenAI function calling API. You describe tools as JSON Schema, the LLM decides when to call them, and your code handles the execution. The LLM never runs the tool — it just outputs the intent.",
            "concepts": [
              "Function Calling",
              "Tool Schema",
