            "question": "Create a simple agent using the OpenAI Agents SDK. Define:\n1. A `get_weather` function tool\n2. An Agent with a name, instructions, and the weather tool\n3. Run the agent with a user query",
            "starterCode": "from agents import Agent, Runner, function_tool\n\n# Step 1: Define a tool\n@___\ndef get_weather(city: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Get the current weather for a city.\"\"\"\n    return f'Weather in {city}: 22°C, Sunny'\n\n# Step 2: Create the agent\nagent = Agent(\n    name='___',\n    instructions='___',\n    tools=[___]\n)\n\n# Step 3: Run it\nresult = Runner.run_sync(agent, 'What is the weather in London?')\nprint(result.final_output)",
            "solution": "from agents import Agent, Runner, function_tool\n\n@function_tool\ndef get_weather(city: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Get the current weather for a city.\"\"\"\n    return f'Weather in {city}: 22°C, Sunny'\n\nagent = Agent(\n    name='Weather Assistant',\n    instructions='You are a helpful weather assistant. Use the get_weather tool to answer weather questions.',\n    tools=[get_weather]\n)\n\nresult = Runner.run_sync(agent, 'What is the weather in London?')\nprint(result.final_output)",
