            "question": "Build a debate system with two agents and a judge. Complete:\n1. Agent A (optimistic) and Agent B (skeptical) generate independent answers\n2. The judge picks the best answer",
            "starterCode": "def llm_call(system_prompt, user_message):\n    return f'[{system_prompt[:30]}] Response to: {user_message[:40]}'\n\ndef debate(question):\n    # Agent A: Optimistic perspective\n    answer_a = llm_call(\n        '___',\n        question\n    )\n    print(f'Agent A: {answer_a}')\n    \n    # Agent B: Skeptical perspective\n    answer_b = llm_call(\n        '___',\n        question\n    )\n    print(f'Agent B: {answer_b}')\n    \n    # Judge: Pick the best\n    verdict = llm_call(\n        'You are a fair judge. Pick the most accurate answer.',\n        f'Question: {question}\\nAnswer A: {___}\\nAnswer B: {___}'\n    )\n    print(f'Judge: {verdict}')\n    \n    return verdict\n\ndebate('Will AI replace software engineers by 2030?')",
            "solution": "def llm_call(system_prompt, user_message):\n    return f'[{system_prompt[:30]}] Response to: {user_message[:40]}'\n\ndef debate(question):\n    answer_a = llm_call(\n        'You are an optimistic analyst. Focus on potential benefits and positive trends.',\n        question\n    )\n    print(f'Agent A: {answer_a}')\n    \n    answer_b = llm_call(\n        'You are a skeptical analyst. Challenge assumptions and highlight risks.',\n        question\n    )\n    print(f'Agent B: {answer_b}')\n    \n    verdict = llm_call(\n        'You are a fair judge. Pick the most accurate answer.',\n        f'Question: {question}\\nAnswer A: {answer_a}\\nAnswer B: {answer_b}'\n    )\n    print(f'Judge: {verdict}')\n    \n    return verdict\n\ndebate('Will AI replace software engineers by 2030?')",
            "hint": "Give Agent A an optimistic system prompt and Agent B a skeptical one. Pass answer_a and answer_b to the judge.",
