            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "HTTP Methods — The 4 Types of Orders",
            "explanation": "Now that you know what an API is, let's learn the language it speaks. When your frontend talks to your backend, it doesn't just send a message — it sends a **type** of message. Think of it like this:\n\nWhen you walk into a restaurant, there are exactly four things you can do with your order. That's it. No matter how fancy the restaurant, these are the only four actions:\n\n**🧒 The Four Types of Orders:**\n\n<img src=\"/images/module 14/m14_http_methods.png\" alt=\"HTTP Methods - The 4 Types of Orders\" />\n\n**1. GET — \"Show me the menu\" (Read)**\nYou're asking the server to SEND you some data. You're not changing anything — just looking.\n```python\n@app.get('/menu')\ndef get_menu():\n    return {'dishes': ['pasta', 'pizza', 'salad']}\n```\n\n**2. POST — \"I'd like to place an order\" (Create)**\nYou're SENDING data to the server to create something new. This is how users submit chat messages, upload files, and create accounts.\n```python\n@app.post('/order')\ndef create_order(dish: str, quantity: int):\n    return {'message': f'Ordered {quantity}x {dish}!'}\n```\n\n**3. PUT — \"Actually, change my order to pasta\" (Update)**\nYou're modifying something that already exists. Like updating your profile picture or editing a saved note.\n```python\n@app.put('/order/42')\ndef update_order(order_id: int, new_dish: str):\n    return {'message': f'Order {order_id} updated to {new_dish}'}\n```\n\n**4. DELETE — \"Cancel my order\" (Delete)**\nYou're telling the server to remove something. Like deleting a chat conversation or removing an account.\n```python\n@app.delete('/order/42')\ndef cancel_order(order_id: int):\n    return {'message': f'Order {order_id} cancelled'}\n```\n\n**💡 The Rule of Thumb:**\n- **GET** = Give me data (safe, repeatable, no side effects)\n- **POST** = Here's new data, do something with it\n- **PUT** = Here's updated data, replace what's there\n- **DELETE** = Remove this data\n\nThis is called **CRUD** — Create (POST), Read (GET), Update (PUT), Delete (DELETE). Every single application you've ever used — Instagram, Spotify, ChatGPT — is just CRUD operations on a database with a pretty frontend on top. Seriously, that's it.\n\n**⚠️ Common Mistake:**\nBeginners often use GET for everything. \"GET /delete-user/42\" — NO! The HTTP method itself should tell you what action is being performed. That's the whole point."
          }
        },
        {
