          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Creating Multiple Endpoints (A Bigger Menu)",
            "explanation": "Your first API had one endpoint. That's like a restaurant with one item on the menu. Not very useful, right? Let's build a real API with multiple endpoints — a bigger menu.\n\n**🧒 The Restaurant Menu Analogy:**\n\nA real restaurant has sections: Appetizers, Main Course, Desserts, Drinks. Each section has multiple items. Your API is the same — you organize endpoints into logical groups, each handling a different type of request.\n\n**Building a Multi-Endpoint API:**\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI(title=\"My AI Assistant API\", version=\"1.0\")\n\n# Health check — is the server alive?\n@app.get('/health')\ndef health_check():\n    return {'status': 'healthy', 'version': '1.0'}\n\n# Get all available AI models\n@app.get('/models')\ndef list_models():\n    return {\n        'models': [\n            {'name': 'gpt-4o', 'type': 'chat', 'cost': '$0.01/1K tokens'},\n            {'name': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'type': 'chat', 'cost': '$0.001/1K tokens'},\n            {'name': 'dall-e-3', 'type': 'image', 'cost': '$0.04/image'}\n        ]\n    }\n\n# Get a specific model's details\n@app.get('/models/{model_name}')\ndef get_model(model_name: str):\n    models = {\n        'gpt-4o': {'name': 'gpt-4o', 'context_window': 128000},\n        'gpt-4o-mini': {'name': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'context_window': 128000}\n    }\n    if model_name not in models:\n        return {'error': f'Model {model_name} not found'}\n    return models[model_name]\n```\n\n**🔍 Path Parameters — The Dynamic Part:**\nNotice `/models/{model_name}`? The curly braces create a **path parameter**. When someone visits `/models/gpt-4o`, FastAPI automatically extracts `\"gpt-4o\"` and passes it to your function as `model_name`. \n\n**Query Parameters — The Optional Filters:**\n```python\n@app.get('/search')\ndef search(query: str, limit: int = 10, language: str = 'en'):\n    return {\n        'query': query,\n        'limit': limit,\n        'language': language,\n        'results': []\n    }\n# Usage: /search?query=AI&limit=5&language=fr\n```\n\nParameters with default values (`limit=10`) are optional. Parameters without defaults (`query`) are required. FastAPI figures this out automatically from your function signature. No configuration files, no decorators, no boilerplate. It just works.\n\n**💡 Pro Tip: Always Start with a Health Check**\nThe `/health` endpoint is the first thing every production API needs. Monitoring tools (like AWS CloudWatch or Uptime Robot) ping this endpoint every 30 seconds to make sure your server is alive. If it stops responding, they alert your team immediately."
          }
        },
