              "explanation": "HNSW (Hierarchical Navigable Small World) indexing enables approximate nearest neighbor search that finds results in 5 milliseconds instead of 10 seconds, with 99%+ accuracy. The LLM model speed is unrelated to vector search speed.",
              "answer": 0
            },
            {
              "question": "You need to store 50 million vectors but only have 20 GB of RAM available. The raw vectors would need 57 GB. Which quantization method is the best starting point?",
              "options": [
                "Binary Quantization — maximum compression",
                "No quantization — buy more RAM",
                "Scalar Quantization (SQ8) — 75% savings with < 1% quality loss",
                "Store vectors on disk instead"
              ],
              "correct": 2,
              "explanation": "Scalar Quantization (SQ8) reduces 57 GB to ~14 GB, fitting within your 20 GB budget with < 1% quality loss. Binary Quantization saves more but loses 5% quality. SQ8 is the safe, recommended starting point.",
              "answer": 2
