        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Multi-Tenant Security — The Enterprise Requirement That Can't Wait",
            "explanation": "Here's a scenario that will give you nightmares if you don't handle it properly.\n\nCompany A and Company B both use your AI platform. Company A uploads confidential merger documents. Without proper isolation, Company B's search might accidentally retrieve Company A's confidential documents.\n\n**This is a data breach. Lawsuit. Regulatory fines. Game over.**\n\n---\n\n**The Wrong Way: Post-Filtering**\n\nYou search ALL vectors first, get the top 100 results, and THEN filter out unauthorized ones.\n\n**Why this is broken:** HNSW search is approximate. If Company B's documents dominate the top 100 results, Company A's relevant documents might not even APPEAR in the results to be filtered. You've both leaked data AND returned bad results.\n\n---\n\n**The Right Way: Pre-Filtering**\n\nFilter by `tenant_id` FIRST, then search ONLY within that tenant's vectors.\n\n```python\n# Qdrant with pre-filtered tenant isolation\nresults = qdrant_client.search(\n    collection_name='documents',\n    query_vector=query_embedding,\n    query_filter=models.Filter(\n        must=[\n            models.FieldCondition(\n                key='tenant_id',\n                match=models.MatchValue(value='company_a')\n            )\n        ]\n    ),\n    limit=5\n)\n```\n\n```sql\n-- pgvector with tenant filtering\nSELECT content, 1 - (embedding <=> $1::vector) AS similarity\nFROM documents\nWHERE tenant_id = 'company_a'\nORDER BY embedding <=> $1::vector\nLIMIT 5;\n```\n\n---\n\n**Document-Level ACLs (Access Control Lists):**\n\nEven within a company, different users have different access levels. A junior employee shouldn't retrieve executive salary documents.\n\n```python\n# Store permission tags as metadata\nindex.upsert(vectors=[{\n    'id': 'doc_secret',\n    'values': embedding,\n    'metadata': {\n        'tenant_id': 'company_a',\n        'access_level': 'executive',     # Only execs can see this\n        'departments': ['finance', 'hr']  # Only these departments\n    }\n}])\n\n# Query with user's permission context\nresults = index.query(\n    vector=query_embedding,\n    filter={\n        'tenant_id': {'$eq': user.tenant_id},\n        'access_level': {'$in': user.access_levels}\n    }\n)\n```\n\n**🔑 The Golden Rule:** ALWAYS filter at the database level, NEVER in your application code. If the database returns unauthorized data to your app — even if your app filters it — the data has already traveled over the network. That's a security vulnerability.",
            "image": "/images/module_15_databases/m15_multi_tenant_security.png"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "mcq",
          "questions": [
            {
              "question": "In a multi-tenant RAG system, why is post-filtering vector search results dangerous?",
              "options": [
                "It's slower than pre-filtering",
                "ANN search is approximate — relevant authorized documents may be displaced by unauthorized ones and never appear in results at all",
