                "score": 20,
                "outcome": "Vector RAG would find documents mentioning 'Client X' or 'projects', but it can't TRAVERSE the chain: People who worked with Client X → Their projects → Technologies used. The connected information is spread across dozens of separate documents."
              },
              {
                "text": "GraphRAG — build a knowledge graph of People, Clients, Projects, and Technologies, then traverse the relationships.",
                "score": 100,
                "outcome": "Correct! This is a multi-hop relationship query. GraphRAG extracts entities and relationships from all 50,000 documents, builds a knowledge graph, and answers by traversing: Client X ← WORKED_WITH → People → MANAGED → Projects → USED → Technologies. The graph connects what individual documents can't."
              },
              {
                "text": "Just use a bigger context window and send all 50,000 documents to GPT-4.",
                "score": 5,
                "outcome": "50,000 documents is far beyond any context window. Even if it fit, the LLM would struggle to connect information scattered across thousands of pages. GraphRAG explicitly models the connections."
              }
