          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "PII Masking & Data Loss Prevention (Microsoft Presidio)",
            "explanation": "Here's a nightmare scenario that has actually happened: a customer pastes their full credit card number into a chatbot asking about a charge. The chatbot, trying to be helpful, includes the credit card number in its response. That response gets logged. Now the credit card number is sitting in your application logs, your analytics dashboard, and possibly your LLM provider's servers.\n\nCongratulations, you've just violated PCI DSS, GDPR, and possibly HIPAA. The fine? Up to $500,000 per incident.\n\n[IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: PII Masking Pipeline Diagram]\n\n** The Redacted FBI Document Analogy:**\n\nYou know those FBI documents where sensitive names and dates are blacked out with marker? That's EXACTLY what PII masking does. Before ANY text reaches the LLM, we scan it and black out (replace) any personal identifiable information.\n\n**What Counts as PII:**\n| PII Type | Example | Risk Level |\n|---|---|---|\n| Social Security Number | 123-45-6789 | Critical |\n| Credit Card Number | 4111-1111-1111-1111 | Critical |\n| Email Address | john@example.com | High |\n| Phone Number | (555) 123-4567 | High |\n| Physical Address | 123 Main St, City, ST 12345 | High |\n| Full Name | John Michael Smith | Medium |\n| Date of Birth | 01/15/1990 | Medium |\n| IP Address | 192.168.1.100 | Medium |\n\n**Microsoft Presidio — The Industry Standard:**\n\nPresidio is Microsoft's open-source PII detection and anonymization engine. It uses a combination of regex patterns, NLP models, and custom recognizers:\n\n```python\nfrom presidio_analyzer import AnalyzerEngine\nfrom presidio_anonymizer import AnonymizerEngine\n\n# Initialize the engines\nanalyzer = AnalyzerEngine()\nanonymizer = AnonymizerEngine()\n\n# Analyze text for PII\ntext = 'My name is John Smith and my SSN is 123-45-6789'\nresults = analyzer.analyze(text=text, language='en')\n\n# Anonymize (replace PII with placeholders)\nanonymized = anonymizer.anonymize(text=text, analyzer_results=results)\nprint(anonymized.text)\n# Output: 'My name is <PERSON> and my SSN is <US_SSN>'\n```\n\n**The PII Masking Pipeline:**\n```\nUser Input → [Presidio Analyzer] → [Presidio Anonymizer] → LLM\n    'My SSN is 123-45-6789'  →  'My SSN is <US_SSN>'  →  LLM sees masked input\n\nLLM Output → [De-anonymize if needed] → [Final PII scan] → User\n```\n\n**Why Mask on BOTH Sides:**\n- **Input masking**: Prevent PII from reaching the LLM provider's servers (GDPR compliance)\n- **Output masking**: Catch cases where the LLM accidentally generates or echoes PII\n\n**Custom Recognizers for Your Domain:**\n```python\nfrom presidio_analyzer import PatternRecognizer, Pattern\n\n# Custom recognizer for your company's internal ID format\ninternal_id_pattern = Pattern(\n    name='internal_id',\n    regex=r'EMP-\\d{6}',  # e.g., EMP-123456\n    score=0.9\n)\n\nrecognizer = PatternRecognizer(\n    supported_entity='INTERNAL_ID',\n    patterns=[internal_id_pattern]\n)\n\nanalyzer.registry.add_recognizer(recognizer)\n```\n\n**The Compliance Checklist:**\n- ✅ GDPR (EU) — Personal data must be anonymized before processing\n- ✅ HIPAA (US Healthcare) — Patient health information must be protected\n- ✅ PCI DSS (Payments) — Credit card data must never be stored in logs\n- ✅ SOC 2 (Enterprise) — Demonstrate data protection controls\n\nWithout PII masking, your AI application is a compliance time bomb. With Presidio, it takes 10 lines of code to defuse it."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
            "language": "python",
            "title": "Building a PII Masking Pipeline with Presidio",
            "difficulty": "Easy",
            "question": "Use Microsoft Presidio to analyze a text string for PII entities and then anonymize (mask) them. The text is: 'Please update the account for Sarah Johnson, email sarah.j@company.com, phone 555-123-4567'",
            "starterCode": "from presidio_analyzer import AnalyzerEngine\nfrom presidio_anonymizer import AnonymizerEngine\n\nanalyzer = AnalyzerEngine()\nanonymizer = AnonymizerEngine()\n\ntext = '___'\n\n# Step 1: Analyze for PII\nresults = analyzer.analyze(text=___, language=___)\n\n# Step 2: Anonymize\nanonymized = anonymizer.anonymize(text=___, analyzer_results=___)\nprint(anonymized.text)",
            "solution": "from presidio_analyzer import AnalyzerEngine\nfrom presidio_anonymizer import AnonymizerEngine\n\nanalyzer = AnalyzerEngine()\nanonymizer = AnonymizerEngine()\n\ntext = 'Please update the account for Sarah Johnson, email sarah.j@company.com, phone 555-123-4567'\n\nresults = analyzer.analyze(text=text, language='en')\n\nanonymized = anonymizer.anonymize(text=text, analyzer_results=results)\nprint(anonymized.text)",
            "hint": "Pass the text variable and 'en' for English language. The anonymize function needs both the original text and the analyzer results.",
            "explanation": "Presidio's two-step process (analyze then anonymize) lets you inspect what PII was found before deciding how to mask it. In production, you'd log the entity types found (for monitoring) while replacing the actual values with safe placeholders.",
            "concepts": [
              "Presidio",
              "PII Masking",
              "Data Loss Prevention"
            ],
            "validation": {
              "type": "regex_match",
              "pattern": "analyzer.analyze.*text.*language.*anonymizer.anonymize.*text.*analyzer_results"
            }
          }
        },
