          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Observability — Seeing Inside Your AI Pipeline",
            "explanation": "When your AI gives a bad response, can you explain WHY? In traditional software, you'd check the logs. But LLM applications have a unique problem: the pipeline has multiple invisible steps, and any one of them could be the culprit.\n\nLet me show you what I mean with a real story.\n\n**The Mystery of the Wrong Answer:**\n\nA user reports: 'Your AI told me my flight is at 3pm, but it's actually at 6pm.' You need to investigate. But WHERE did it go wrong?\n\n[IMAGE:/images/m17/m17_llm_observability.png]\n\n** The Hospital X-Ray Analogy:**\n\nImagine a patient comes to the ER with stomach pain. The doctor could guess what's wrong (prompt engineering). Or they could take an X-ray and SEE exactly what's happening inside (observability). \n\nObservability is the X-ray machine for your AI pipeline. It lets you see EVERY step:\n\n```\nUser Query: 'When is my flight?'\n    │\n    ├─ Step 1: Query Rewriting (0.2s, $0.001)\n    │   Input: 'When is my flight?'\n    │   Output: 'flight departure time user_id=12345'\n    │\n    ├─ Step 2: RAG Retrieval (0.5s, $0.003)\n    │   Retrieved: booking_confirmation_v2.pdf (score: 0.87)\n    │   ⚠️ Retrieved OUTDATED document (v2, not v3!)\n    │\n    ├─ Step 3: LLM Generation (1.2s, $0.008)\n    │   Prompt: 'Based on this booking: ... Answer: ...'\n    │   Output: 'Your flight is at 3pm'  ← Wrong! V3 says 6pm\n    │\n    └─ Total: 1.9s, $0.012, ❌ Incorrect Answer\n```\n\nNow you can see it! The retriever pulled an OUTDATED document (v2 instead of v3). The LLM faithfully read the old document and gave the old time. The LLM did its job perfectly — the bug was in the retriever.\n\nWithout observability, you'd be guessing for hours. With it, you found the root cause in 30 seconds.\n\n**The Three Pillars of LLM Observability:**\n\n**1. Tracing (The Most Important):**\nA trace captures the complete execution path of a single request, including every chain step, tool call, LLM invocation, and retrieval:\n\n```python\nimport langsmith\n\n# Enable tracing (just set env vars!)\nos.environ['LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2'] = 'true'\nos.environ['LANGCHAIN_API_KEY'] = 'your-key'\nos.environ['LANGCHAIN_PROJECT'] = 'production-chatbot'\n\n# Now every chain execution is automatically traced\nresult = chain.invoke({'question': user_query})\n# → Full trace visible in LangSmith dashboard\n```\n\n**2. Metrics (The Dashboard):**\n```python\n# Key metrics to track\nmetrics = {\n    'latency_p50': '1.2s',      # Median response time\n    'latency_p99': '4.8s',      # Worst-case response time  \n    'token_cost_per_query': '$0.012',  # Average cost\n    'error_rate': '0.3%',       # Percentage of failed requests\n    'hallucination_rate': '2.1%', # From automated eval\n    'user_satisfaction': '4.2/5'  # From feedback\n}\n```\n\n**3. Logging (The Audit Trail):**\n```python\nimport structlog\nlogger = structlog.get_logger()\n\nlogger.info('llm_request',\n    user_id='u123',\n    model='gpt-4o-mini',\n    input_tokens=150,\n    output_tokens=89,\n    latency_ms=1200,\n    cost_usd=0.012,\n    guardrail_triggered=False\n)\n```\n\n**Popular Observability Tools:**\n| Tool | Best For | Open Source? |\n|---|---|---|\n| **LangSmith** | LangChain ecosystem, full-featured | Freemium |\n| **LangFuse** | Open-source alternative to LangSmith | Yes |\n| **Arize Phoenix** | ML + LLM observability | Yes |\n| **Datadog LLM** | Enterprise monitoring integration | No |\n| **Helicone** | Simple API proxy for logging | Freemium |\n\n**The Golden Rule of Observability:**\nIf you can't see it, you can't fix it. If you can't measure it, you can't improve it. Every production LLM application needs tracing from day one."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "visual",
          "content": {
