        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Cost Optimization — Cutting LLM Costs by 80%",
            "explanation": "Let's talk about the elephant in the room. You've built an amazing AI application. Users love it. Your manager is thrilled. Then the first monthly API bill arrives.\n\n$47,000.\n\nFor a chatbot.\n\nThis is not hypothetical. I've seen startups burn through their entire seed funding on OpenAI API costs because nobody thought about optimization. Let me show you how to slash that bill by 80% without sacrificing quality.\n\n[IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: LLM Cost Optimization Strategies]\n\n** The Electricity Bill Analogy:**\n\nImagine your house has every light, every appliance, and every heater running 24/7. Your electricity bill would be insane. But a smart homeowner:\n- Turns off lights in empty rooms (model routing)\n- Uses LED bulbs instead of incandescent (smaller models)\n- Installs a thermostat that learns your schedule (semantic caching)\n- Gets solar panels for predictable energy (self-hosting)\n\nLLM cost optimization works the same way.\n\n**The Cost Equation:**\n```\nCost = (Input Tokens + Output Tokens) × Price per Token × Number of Requests\n```\n\nLet's break down each lever:\n\n**Strategy 1: Model Routing (Save 60-80%)**\n\nNot every query needs GPT-4. Most questions can be answered by a model that's 10x cheaper:\n\n```python\nasync def smart_route(query: str) -> str:\n    complexity = classify_complexity(query)  # Use a tiny classifier\n    \n    if complexity == 'simple':\n        # 'What are your hours?' -> GPT-4o-mini ($0.15/1M tokens)\n        return await call_model('gpt-4o-mini', query)\n    elif complexity == 'medium':\n        # 'Compare your plans' -> Claude Haiku ($0.25/1M tokens)\n        return await call_model('claude-3-haiku', query)\n    else:\n        # 'Debug this complex code' -> GPT-4o ($2.50/1M tokens)\n        return await call_model('gpt-4o', query)\n```\n\n**Real savings:** If 70% of queries are simple, 20% medium, 10% complex:\n- Before: 100% GPT-4o = $2.50/1M × all queries\n- After: 70% mini + 20% haiku + 10% GPT-4o = ~$0.50/1M average\n- **Savings: 80%!**\n\n**Strategy 2: Prompt Optimization (Save 20-40%)**\n\nShorter prompts = fewer tokens = lower cost:\n```python\n# EXPENSIVE (847 tokens)\nprompt_v1 = '''You are an incredibly helpful AI assistant \nthat has been specifically designed and trained to help \nusers with their questions about our amazing products...'''\n\n# CHEAP (124 tokens) - Same quality!\nprompt_v2 = '''You are a product support agent. Answer \nconcisely using the provided context. If unsure, say so.'''\n```\n\n**Strategy 3: Caching (Save 30-50%)**\n\nIf 100 users ask 'What are your business hours?', why pay for 100 LLM calls? Cache the answer after the first one.\n\n**Strategy 4: Batch Processing (Save 50%)**\n\nOpenAI offers 50% discounts for batch API calls (non-real-time):\n```python\n# Real-time: $5.00/1M input tokens (GPT-4o)\n# Batch: $2.50/1M input tokens (50% off!)\n```\n\nPerfect for nightly evaluation runs, bulk document processing, and report generation.\n\n**The Cost Optimization Decision Tree:**\n| Question | If Yes | Savings |\n|---|---|---|\n| Is the query simple? | Route to cheap model | 60-80% |\n| Has this been asked before? | Serve from cache | 100% (free) |\n| Is it non-urgent? | Use batch API | 50% |\n| Is the prompt too long? | Compress it | 20-40% |\n| Can you self-host? | Use open-source model | 70-90% long-term |"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Unified AI Gateways (LiteLLM / Portkey) for Multi-Provider Routing",
            "explanation": "Here's a problem you'll hit the moment you start using multiple LLM providers (and you should): each provider has a different API format, different authentication, different error codes, and different rate limits.\n\nYou call OpenAI with `openai.chat.completions.create()`. You call Anthropic with `anthropic.messages.create()`. You call Google with `genai.generate_content()`. Three different libraries, three different interfaces, three sets of API keys.\n\nNow imagine your code has 47 places where it calls an LLM. And you want to switch from GPT-4 to Claude for half of them. You'd have to rewrite 23 call sites. That's a nightmare.\n\n[IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: AI Gateway Architecture]\n\n** The Universal Power Adapter Analogy:**\n\nWhen you travel internationally, every country has a different plug shape. You could carry 10 different adapters, or you could carry ONE universal adapter that works everywhere.\n\nAn AI Gateway is the universal adapter for LLMs. You write ONE API call, and the gateway routes it to any provider.\n\n**LiteLLM — The Open-Source Gateway:**\n\n```python\nfrom litellm import completion\n\n# Same function, ANY provider!\nresponse = completion(\n    model='gpt-4o',  # OpenAI\n    messages=[{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Hello!'}]\n)\n\nresponse = completion(\n    model='claude-3-sonnet-20240229',  # Anthropic\n    messages=[{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Hello!'}]\n)\n\nresponse = completion(\n    model='gemini/gemini-pro',  # Google\n    messages=[{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Hello!'}]\n)\n```\n\n**One function call. 100+ models. Zero code changes.**\n\n**Why AI Gateways Are Essential:**\n\n1. **Provider Failover**: If OpenAI goes down, automatically switch to Anthropic\n```python\nresponse = completion(\n    model='gpt-4o',\n    messages=messages,\n    fallbacks=['claude-3-sonnet', 'gemini-pro']  # Automatic failover!\n)\n```\n\n2. **Cost-Based Routing**: Route to the cheapest provider that meets quality requirements\n\n3. **Rate Limit Management**: When you hit OpenAI's rate limit, overflow to Anthropic\n\n4. **Unified Logging**: One log format for all providers\n\n5. **A/B Testing**: Route 50% to GPT-4o and 50% to Claude for comparison\n\n**Setting Up LiteLLM as a Proxy Server:**\n```yaml\n# litellm_config.yaml\nmodel_list:\n  - model_name: production-chat\n    litellm_params:\n      model: gpt-4o-mini\n      api_key: sk-xxx\n  - model_name: production-chat  # Same name = load balancing!\n    litellm_params:\n      model: claude-3-haiku-20240307\n      api_key: sk-ant-xxx\n  - model_name: premium-chat\n    litellm_params:\n      model: gpt-4o\n      api_key: sk-xxx\n```\n\n```bash\n# Start the gateway\nlitellm --config litellm_config.yaml --port 4000\n```\n\nNow your entire application calls `localhost:4000` with the OpenAI format, and LiteLLM handles routing, failover, and load balancing behind the scenes.\n\n**Portkey — The Managed Alternative:**\n\nIf you don't want to self-host, Portkey provides the same gateway functionality as a managed service with additional features like budget alerts, request caching, and compliance controls."
          }
        },
