            "question": "Calculate the VRAM savings from quantizing a model. Write a function that takes the number of parameters (in billions) and returns a dictionary with the model size in GB at FP16 (16-bit), INT8 (8-bit), and INT4 (4-bit).",
            "starterCode": "def calculate_model_sizes(params_billions: float) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Calculate model sizes at different quantization levels.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'fp16_gb': params_billions * ___ / 1,  # 2 bytes per param\n        'int8_gb': params_billions * ___ / 1,  # 1 byte per param  \n        'int4_gb': params_billions * ___ / 1,  # 0.5 bytes per param\n    }\n\n# Test with Llama 8B\nsizes = calculate_model_sizes(8)\nprint(f\"FP16: {sizes['fp16_gb']:.1f} GB\")\nprint(f\"INT8: {sizes['int8_gb']:.1f} GB\")\nprint(f\"INT4: {sizes['int4_gb']:.1f} GB\")",
