            "hint": "FP16 = 2 bytes per parameter, INT8 = 1 byte, INT4 = 0.5 bytes. Multiply by billions of params.",
            "explanation": "An 8B parameter model at FP16 is 16 GB (8 billion × 2 bytes). At INT4, it's only 4 GB (8 billion × 0.5 bytes). This 4x reduction is what makes it possible to run large models on consumer GPUs.",
