          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Production Resilience — When Things Go Wrong",
            "explanation": "Production systems WILL fail. That's not pessimism — that's engineering reality. The difference between a good engineer and a great engineer isn't preventing ALL failures (impossible). It's building systems that HANDLE failures gracefully.\n\n** The Hospital Emergency Room Analogy:**\n\nAn ER doesn't prevent all emergencies. Instead, it's DESIGNED to handle them:\n- **Triage** → Prioritize critical cases (error classification)\n- **Backup generators** → Power stays on even during outages (failover)\n- **Multiple doctors** → If one is busy, another takes over (redundancy)\n- **Escalation protocols** → Know when to call a specialist (graceful degradation)\n\nYour LLM production system needs the same design.\n\n**The 5 Most Common Production Failures:**\n\n**1. API Rate Limiting**\n```python\n# You exceeded the provider's request limit\n# Solution: Exponential backoff with jitter\nimport tenacity\n\n@tenacity.retry(\n    wait=tenacity.wait_exponential(multiplier=1, max=60),\n    stop=tenacity.stop_after_attempt(5),\n    retry=tenacity.retry_if_exception_type(RateLimitError)\n)\ndef call_llm(messages):\n    return openai.chat.completions.create(\n        model='gpt-4o-mini', messages=messages\n    )\n```\n\n**2. Provider Outage**\n```python\n# OpenAI is down? Fail over to Anthropic.\nasync def resilient_call(messages):\n    providers = [\n        ('gpt-4o-mini', call_openai),\n        ('claude-3-haiku', call_anthropic),\n        ('gemini-flash', call_google)\n    ]\n    for model, call_fn in providers:\n        try:\n            return await call_fn(model, messages)\n        except ProviderError:\n            logger.warning(f'{model} failed, trying next provider')\n            continue\n    return fallback_response()  # Static response as last resort\n```\n\n**3. Context Window Overflow**\n```python\n# Input exceeded the model's token limit\ndef safe_truncate(text: str, max_tokens: int = 120000):\n    tokens = tokenizer.encode(text)\n    if len(tokens) > max_tokens:\n        tokens = tokens[:max_tokens]\n        logger.warning(f'Truncated input from {len(tokens)} to {max_tokens}')\n    return tokenizer.decode(tokens)\n```\n\n**4. Invalid Output Format**\n```python\n# LLM didn't follow structured output format\nimport json\n\ndef parse_json_response(response: str, retries: int = 3):\n    for attempt in range(retries):\n        try:\n            return json.loads(response)\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            # Ask the LLM to fix its own output\n            response = llm(f'Fix this invalid JSON: {response}')\n    return {'error': 'Failed to parse response', 'raw': response}\n```\n\n**5. Hallucination Detection**\n```python\n# Check if response is grounded in context\ndef hallucination_check(response: str, context: str) -> bool:\n    check = llm(\n        f'Is this response fully supported by the context?\\n'\n        f'Context: {context}\\n'\n        f'Response: {response}\\n'\n        f'Answer YES or NO only.'\n    )\n    return 'YES' in check.upper()\n```\n\n**The Resilience Pattern Stack:**\n| Pattern | What It Handles | Implementation |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Retry with Backoff** | Transient errors, rate limits | tenacity library |\n| **Provider Failover** | Provider outages | Fallback chain |\n| **Circuit Breaker** | Sustained failures | Stop calling after N failures |\n| **Graceful Degradation** | Partial failures | Return cached/simplified response |\n| **Timeout** | Slow responses | Kill after N seconds |\n\n**The Golden Rule:**\nEvery external call (LLM API, database, vector store) should have: a timeout, a retry strategy, a fallback, and logging. No exceptions."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "challenge": {
