          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Practice Project: End-to-End LLMOps Pipeline",
            "explanation": "**Your Mission:**\n\nBuild a production-ready AI Q&A system with full LLMOps instrumentation. This project ties together EVERYTHING from this module into one cohesive system.\n\n**What You Will Build:**\nA \"Company Knowledge Base Q&A System\" that answers employee questions using RAG, with full production guardrails, evaluation, caching, and observability.\n\n**Architecture:**\n```\nUser Question\n    │\n    ├─ [1. Input Guardrails] → PII masking, injection detection\n    │\n    ├─ [2. Semantic Cache Check] → Return cached answer if available\n    │\n    ├─ [3. Model Router] → Route to cheap/expensive model based on complexity\n    │\n    ├─ [4. RAG Retrieval] → Fetch relevant documents\n    │\n    ├─ [5. LLM Generation] → Generate answer (with tracing)\n    │\n    ├─ [6. Output Guardrails] → Hallucination check, content safety\n    │\n    ├─ [7. RAG Triad Evaluation] → Score faithfulness + relevance\n    │\n    └─ [8. Response + Feedback UI] → Thumbs up/down for data flywheel\n```\n\n**Project Requirements:**\n\n1. **Input Pipeline** (Guardrails):\n   - Prompt injection detection (keyword + semantic)\n   - PII masking with Presidio\n   - Topic boundary enforcement\n\n2. **Cost Optimization**:\n   - Semantic caching with Redis (or in-memory fallback)\n   - Model routing based on query complexity\n   - Token usage tracking\n\n3. **RAG + Generation**:\n   - Vector store with sample company documents\n   - LLM generation with structured output\n   - Retrieval context logging\n\n4. **Output Pipeline** (Safety):\n   - Hallucination detection (grounding check)\n   - Content safety filter\n   - PII output scan\n\n5. **Evaluation & Observability**:\n   - RAG Triad scoring on every response\n   - Full request tracing (input → retrieval → generation → output)\n   - Cost tracking per request\n   - Quality dashboard metrics\n\n6. **Feedback Loop**:\n   - Thumbs up/down collection\n   - Weekly export of low-rated responses for review\n   - Training data extraction from expert corrections\n\n**Suggested Tech Stack:**\n| Component | Tool |\n|---|---|\n| LLM | OpenAI GPT-4o-mini (API) or Ollama (local) |\n| Vector Store | ChromaDB or FAISS |\n| Caching | Redis or Python dict (prototype) |\n| Guardrails | Presidio + custom filters |\n| Evaluation | DeepEval or Ragas |\n| Observability | LangSmith or LangFuse |\n| Gateway | LiteLLM |\n\n**Evaluation Criteria:**\n- Does the system have input AND output guardrails?\n- Does semantic caching reduce redundant LLM calls?\n- Is every request traced with full observability?\n- Does the RAG Triad evaluation catch hallucinations?\n- Is there a feedback mechanism for continuous improvement?\n\n**Stretch Goals:**\n- Add A/B testing for two different prompts\n- Implement a CI/CD evaluation pipeline with GitHub Actions\n- Add NeMo Guardrails with Colang rules\n- Build a simple dashboard showing quality metrics over time\n\nThis project is your proof that you can build production-grade AI systems, not just prototypes. Good luck!"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
