      "id": "M018-production-system-design",
      "title": "Module 18: Production AI System Design",
      "stages": [
        {
          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "What Does 'Production' Actually Mean?",
            "explanation": "You've built amazing AI projects throughout this course — chatbots, RAG systems, agents, and more. But there's a huge difference between a project that works on YOUR laptop and one that works for THOUSANDS of users 24/7.\n\n**Think of it like cooking:**\n- Building a prototype = cooking dinner for yourself. If you burn the garlic, no big deal.\n- Going to production = running a restaurant. Hundreds of customers expect consistent quality, the kitchen can't go down during rush hour, and health inspectors check your safety standards.\n\n**A production AI system must handle 3 things:**\n\n1. **Reliability** — It works 99.9% of the time. When the LLM API goes down at 3 AM, the system handles it gracefully instead of showing users a blank screen.\n\n2. **Scalability** — It handles 10 users today and 10,000 users tomorrow without rewriting everything. The architecture grows WITH your user base.\n\n3. **Security** — User data is protected. Prompt injection attacks are blocked. PII (Personally Identifiable Information) never leaks. Compliance requirements (GDPR, HIPAA) are met.\n\n**Why Prototypes Fail in Production:**\n\n• No error handling → one API timeout crashes everything\n• No caching → you pay $100/day in LLM costs for repeated queries\n• No rate limiting → one aggressive user takes down your service\n• No monitoring → you don't know something's broken until users complain\n• Hardcoded API keys → security breach waiting to happen\n\nThis module teaches you how to take everything you've built and make it production-ready. We'll start simple and progressively add enterprise-grade features."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "mcq",
          "questions": [
            {
              "question": "What are the 3 key requirements for a production AI system?",
              "options": [
                "Speed, beauty, simplicity",
                "Reliability, scalability, security",
                "Cost, features, documentation",
                "Testing, deployment, monitoring"
              ],
              "answer": 1,
              "explanation": "The 3 pillars of production systems are: Reliability (it works 99.9% of the time), Scalability (it handles growing traffic), and Security (user data is protected and attacks are blocked)."
            },
            {
              "question": "Why do most AI prototypes fail when put into production?",
              "options": [
                "The AI model is too slow",
                "They lack error handling, caching, rate limiting, and monitoring",
                "Python is not suitable for production",
                "LLM APIs don't work outside localhost"
              ],
