          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Your First Production-Ready Setup",
            "explanation": "Let's take a basic FastAPI + OpenAI app and add the minimum production essentials. These 5 additions transform a fragile prototype into something you can actually deploy:\n\n**1. Environment Variables (never hardcode secrets):**\nStore API keys, database URLs, and config in `.env` files. Use `python-dotenv` or Pydantic Settings to load them. NEVER commit secrets to Git.\n\n**2. Health Checks (know if your app is alive):**\nA `/health` endpoint that returns `{\"status\": \"healthy\"}`. Load balancers and Kubernetes use this to know if your app is running. If the health check fails, the system automatically restarts it.\n\n**3. Structured Logging (know what happened):**\nReplace `print()` with proper logging. Use JSON-formatted logs with timestamps, request IDs, and log levels (INFO, WARNING, ERROR). When something breaks at 3 AM, logs are your detective.\n\n**4. Error Handling (don't crash on failures):**\nWrap LLM API calls in try/except blocks. If OpenAI returns a 500 error, retry with exponential backoff. If it's still down, return a friendly error message instead of a stack trace.\n\n**5. CORS Configuration (let your frontend talk to your backend):**\nConfigure Cross-Origin Resource Sharing so your React frontend (running on port 3000) can call your FastAPI backend (running on port 8000). Without this, browsers block the requests.\n\nThese 5 things take about 30 minutes to add but prevent 90% of production failures."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
