          "type": "concept",
          "content": {
            "title": "Model Routing: The Smart Traffic Director",
            "explanation": "Not every question deserves the most expensive AI model. Sending 'Hi, how are you?' to GPT-4o costs 16x more than GPT-4o-mini — for the same quality answer.\n\n**How Model Routing Works:**\n\n1. **Complexity-Based Routing** — A classifier categorizes each query:\n   - Simple (greetings, yes/no) -> GPT-4o-mini ($0.15/M tokens)\n   - Complex (reasoning, code, analysis) -> GPT-4o ($2.50/M tokens)\n\n2. **Cost-Based Routing** — Set per-user budgets, downgrade to cheaper models when budget is nearly exhausted.\n\n3. **Latency-Based Routing** — Route to the fastest provider for real-time apps.\n\n4. **Capability-Based Routing** — Match tasks to model strengths:\n   - Code -> Claude (best at coding)\n   - Long docs -> Gemini (2M token window)\n   - Creative -> GPT-4o\n\n5. **Fallback Chains** — Primary -> Secondary -> Emergency backup\n   GPT-4o -> Azure GPT-4o -> Claude -> cached response\n\n**Impact:** 60-80% cost reduction while maintaining quality."
          }
        },
