            "question": "Complete the route() method. Use classify_query() to determine complexity, then return the appropriate model name from self.models.",
            "starterCode": "class ModelRouter:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.models = {\n            \"simple\": \"gpt-4o-mini\",\n            \"complex\": \"gpt-4o\",\n        }\n    \n    def classify_query(self, query):\n        complex_keywords = [\"analyze\", \"compare\", \"explain in detail\", \"code\", \"debug\"]\n        if any(kw in query.lower() for kw in complex_keywords) or len(query) > 200:\n            return \"complex\"\n        return \"simple\"\n    \n    def route(self, query):\n        # TODO: Classify and return the right model\n        pass\n\nrouter = ModelRouter()\nprint(router.route(\"Hello!\"))\nprint(router.route(\"Analyze this code and explain the bug\"))",
            "solution": "class ModelRouter:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.models = {\n            \"simple\": \"gpt-4o-mini\",\n            \"complex\": \"gpt-4o\",\n        }\n    \n    def classify_query(self, query):\n        complex_keywords = [\"analyze\", \"compare\", \"explain in detail\", \"code\", \"debug\"]\n        if any(kw in query.lower() for kw in complex_keywords) or len(query) > 200:\n            return \"complex\"\n        return \"simple\"\n    \n    def route(self, query):\n        category = self.classify_query(query)\n        return self.models.get(category, self.models[\"simple\"])\n\nrouter = ModelRouter()\nprint(router.route(\"Hello!\"))\nprint(router.route(\"Analyze this code and explain the bug\"))",
            "hint": "Call self.classify_query(query) then look up in self.models with a fallback.",
