            "question": "What is the main advantage of continuous batching over traditional static batching in LLM serving?",
            "options": [
              "It uses less GPU memory by compressing model weights",
              "It allows new requests to fill completed slots immediately, keeping GPU utilization near 100%",
              "It reduces the number of GPUs needed by splitting the model across CPUs",
              "It caches all previous responses to avoid recomputation"
            ],
            "correctAnswer": 1,
            "explanation": "Continuous batching dynamically adds new requests as soon as existing requests finish generating tokens. Unlike static batching (where all requests in a batch must complete before new ones start), continuous batching keeps the GPU busy at all times, increasing throughput 5-10x."
