            "correctAnswer": 1,
            "explanation": "Since you already run PostgreSQL, pgvector is the most pragmatic choice. It adds vector search capability to your existing database with a single 'CREATE EXTENSION vector' command. No new infrastructure to manage, no data sync issues, and 50K documents is well within pgvector's performance sweet spot."
          }
