            "title": "Write a DeepEval Test for RAG Faithfulness",
            "difficulty": "Hard",
            "question": "Write a DeepEval test that:\n1. Creates an LLMTestCase with input, actual_output, and retrieval_context\n2. Uses FaithfulnessMetric with threshold 0.8\n3. Asserts the test case passes\n4. The input is 'What are Docker volumes?'\n5. The retrieval_context is ['Docker volumes are persistent storage...']",
            "starterCode": "from deepeval import assert_test\nfrom deepeval.test_case import LLMTestCase\nfrom deepeval.metrics import FaithfulnessMetric\n\ndef test_rag_faithfulness():\n    test_case = LLMTestCase(\n        input=___,\n        actual_output=get_rag_response(\"What are Docker volumes?\"),\n        retrieval_context=___\n    )\n    \n    metric = FaithfulnessMetric(threshold=___)\n    assert_test(test_case, [___])",
            "solution": "from deepeval import assert_test\nfrom deepeval.test_case import LLMTestCase\nfrom deepeval.metrics import FaithfulnessMetric\n\ndef test_rag_faithfulness():\n    test_case = LLMTestCase(\n        input=\"What are Docker volumes?\",\n        actual_output=get_rag_response(\"What are Docker volumes?\"),\n        retrieval_context=[\"Docker volumes are persistent storage...\"]\n    )\n    \n    metric = FaithfulnessMetric(threshold=0.8)\n    assert_test(test_case, [metric])",
            "hints": [
              "Input and retrieval_context are strings/lists",
