              {
                "text": "Activate the circuit breaker to route overflowing requests to the local Llama 3 model, while continuing to send requests within rate limits to OpenAI",
                "feedback": "Perfect! The circuit breaker detects the high failure rate (60%) and opens, routing excess traffic to the local Ollama backup. Users within the rate limit still get GPT-4 quality, while overflow users get Llama 3 responses (slightly lower quality but functional). No one gets an error page.",
                "isCorrect": true
              },
              {
                "text": "Immediately switch ALL traffic to the local Llama 3 model and stop using OpenAI entirely",
                "feedback": "This works but is too aggressive — the 40% of requests that ARE succeeding on OpenAI deliver better quality. The optimal approach is to use both: send what you can to OpenAI, overflow to local. Once OpenAI recovers, the circuit breaker automatically re-closes.",
                "isCorrect": false
              }
            ]
          }
        },
